window.BCG_PAGES = {"index":{"slug":"index","title":"Belief Context Graph","description":"Belief-native graph memory for LLM agents: probabilistic, temporal, evidence-grounded, and auditable.","html":"\n<section aria-labelledby=\"motifTitle\" class=\"belief-motif motif-v12\" data-active-kind=\"evidence\">\n<div class=\"motif-copy\">\n<div class=\"motif-heading\">\n<span class=\"eyebrow\">Typed graph memory</span>\n<h2 class=\"motif-title\" id=\"motifTitle\">From evidence to belief, then decision</h2>\n</div>\n<div class=\"motif-intro\">\n<p class=\"motif-summary\">\n        Evidence preserves exact provenance. Beliefs turn it into typed\n        propositions, and decisions specialize a belief for an action,\n        judgment, or conclusion.\n      </p>\n<p class=\"motif-instruction\">Select an element to inspect its role.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div aria-label=\"Evidence, belief, and decision\" class=\"motif-flow\" role=\"group\">\n<button aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"motif-inspectable motif-card motif-evidence selected\" data-default=\"true\" data-description=\"Exact provenance with source offsets. Evidence is not a graph node and may come from user, assistant, tool, or function turns.\" data-kind=\"evidence\" data-title=\"Evidence record\" type=\"button\">\n<span class=\"motif-card-top\">\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"motif-card-icon\">\n<svg fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\">\n<path d=\"M6 3h9l4 4v14H6V3Z\"></path>\n<path d=\"M15 3v5h5M9 12h6M9 16h5\"></path>\n</svg>\n</span>\n<span class=\"motif-step\">01 · record</span>\n</span>\n<strong>Evidence</strong>\n<span class=\"motif-card-description\">Exact provenance</span>\n<span class=\"motif-card-meta\">not a node · any turn role</span>\n</button>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"motif-connector motif-grounds\">\n<span>grounds</span><i></i>\n</div>\n<button aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"motif-inspectable motif-card motif-belief\" data-description=\"A typed proposition carrying canonical text, stance, layer, confidence, provenance, and evidence references.\" data-kind=\"belief\" data-title=\"Belief node\" type=\"button\">\n<span class=\"motif-card-top\">\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"motif-card-icon\">\n<svg fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\">\n<path d=\"M9.5 4.5A3 3 0 0 0 4 6a3 3 0 0 0 .7 5.9A3 3 0 0 0 7 17.5h2.5V4.5Z\"></path>\n<path d=\"M14.5 4.5A3 3 0 0 1 20 6a3 3 0 0 1-.7 5.9 3 3 0 0 1-2.3 5.6h-2.5V4.5Z\"></path>\n<path d=\"M9.5 8H7.8M14.5 8h1.7M9.5 12H7M14.5 12h2.5\"></path>\n</svg>\n</span>\n<span class=\"motif-step\">02 · node</span>\n</span>\n<strong>Belief</strong>\n<span class=\"motif-card-description\">Typed proposition</span>\n<span class=\"motif-card-meta\">confidence · stance · layer</span>\n</button>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"motif-connector motif-specializes\">\n<span>specializes</span><i></i>\n</div>\n<button aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"motif-inspectable motif-card motif-decision\" data-description=\"A specialized belief node using node_type='decision' for an action, judgment, or conclusion.\" data-kind=\"decision\" data-title=\"Decision node\" type=\"button\">\n<span class=\"motif-card-top\">\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"motif-card-icon\">\n<svg fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\">\n<path d=\"m5 12 4 4L19 6\"></path>\n</svg>\n</span>\n<span class=\"motif-step\">03 · specialized</span>\n</span>\n<strong>Decision</strong>\n<span class=\"motif-card-description\">Action or conclusion</span>\n<span class=\"motif-card-meta\">a specialized belief</span>\n</button>\n</div>\n<div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"motif-readout\">\n<span class=\"motif-readout-label\">Selected element</span>\n<div class=\"motif-readout-copy\">\n<strong id=\"motifReadoutTitle\">Evidence record</strong>\n<p id=\"motifReadout\">\n        Exact provenance with source offsets. Evidence is not a graph node and\n        may come from user, assistant, tool, or function turns.\n      </p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-LsSf<span class=\"w\"> </span>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigai-nlco/belief-context-graph/main/install.sh<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>sh\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>--version</code></pre></div>\n<p>Most agent memory systems are optimized for retrieval: preserving conversation history, finding similar fragments, linking entities, or recording what happened. An agent can retrieve the right passage and still act on the wrong belief.</p>\n<p>Those systems answer retrieval questions—<em>what is relevant, what is related, and what happened?</em> BCG addresses the next layer: what the agent should believe and whether confidence is sufficient to act.</p><p>The missing questions are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Should the agent believe this claim?</li>\n<li>How confident should it be?</li>\n<li>Which exact evidence supports it?</li>\n<li>What contradicts or qualifies it?</li>\n<li>Was it formed in this session or inherited from an earlier one?</li>\n<li>Is uncertainty high enough to block action?</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Belief Context Graph (<code>BCG</code>) upgrades agent memory from retrieval memory to belief computation memory.</strong> It turns an agent trajectory into a graph of beliefs, decisions, evidence, confidence, and typed relations. BCG is agent-independent: use the included terminal Agent, embed the Python SDK, or call the streaming HTTP server from your own runtime.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-bcg-adds\">What BCG adds</h2>\n<div class=\"doc-card-grid cols-2\"><div class=\"doc-card static\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M9.5 4.5A3 3 0 0 0 4 6a3 3 0 0 0 .7 5.9A3 3 0 0 0 7 17.5h2.5V4.5Z\"></path><path d=\"M14.5 4.5A3 3 0 0 1 20 6a3 3 0 0 1-.7 5.9 3 3 0 0 1-2.3 5.6h-2.5V4.5Z\"></path><path d=\"M9.5 8H7.8M14.5 8h1.7M9.5 12H7M14.5 12h2.5M9.5 16H8M14.5 16h1.5\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Belief-native memory</strong><p>Store beliefs and decisions as first-class typed nodes rather than anonymous chunks.</p></span></div><div class=\"doc-card static\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 16a8 8 0 1 1 16 0\"></path><path d=\"m12 16 5-6\"></path><path d=\"M7 16h10\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Deterministic confidence</strong><p>Recompute posterior confidence from an explicit prior, merged evidence, and active graph factors.</p></span></div><div class=\"doc-card static\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m9 11-5 5v4h4l5-5\"></path><path d=\"m13 15 7-7-4-4-7 7 4 4Z\"></path><path d=\"M4 20h16\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Exact provenance</strong><p>Link every extracted belief back to character offsets in its source turn.</p></span></div><div class=\"doc-card static\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 8V4m0 0h4M4 4l3 3\"></path><path d=\"M5.5 9A8 8 0 1 1 4 14\"></path><path d=\"M12 8v4l3 2\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Temporal state</strong><p>Track sessions, turns, event time, merge history, and confidence history.</p></span></div><div class=\"doc-card static\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect height=\"5\" rx=\"1\" width=\"6\" x=\"3\" y=\"4\"></rect><rect height=\"5\" rx=\"1\" width=\"6\" x=\"15\" y=\"4\"></rect><rect height=\"5\" rx=\"1\" width=\"6\" x=\"9\" y=\"15\"></rect><path d=\"M6 9v2h12V9M12 11v4\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Conflict-aware relations</strong><p>Represent dependency, supplementation, and contradiction explicitly.</p></span></div><div class=\"doc-card static\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"6\"></circle><path d=\"m14.5 14.5 5 5\"></path><path d=\"M7 12V9m3 3V7m3 5v-2\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Auditable execution</strong><p>Inspect prompts, embedding calls, merge decisions, timing, token usage, and graph evolution.</p></span></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"the-core-loop\">The core loop</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">conversation turn\n      │\n      ▼\nsplit or semantic chunk\n      │\n      ▼\nextract beliefs + decisions + evidence\n      │\n      ▼\ninitialize confidence\n      │\n      ▼\nmerge duplicates before linking\n      │\n      ▼\ncreate typed relations\n      │\n      ▼\npropagate relation confidence\n      │\n      ▼\nqueryable BCG + audit artifacts</code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout note\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M6 3h9l4 4v14H6V3Z\"></path><path d=\"M15 3v5h5M9 12h6M9 16h5\"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Note</strong><p>BCG does not replace an agent framework. It supplies graph construction, a typed graph model, context assembly, HTTP endpoints, artifacts, and reference integrations beneath your existing agent loop.</p></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"start-by-use-case\">Start by use case</h2>\n<div class=\"doc-card-grid cols-2\"><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/reference-agent\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" width=\"18\" x=\"3\" y=\"4\"></rect><path d=\"m7 9 3 3-3 3M12 15h5\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Try the reference Agent</strong><p>Launch the bundled terminal Agent and switch between Default and BCG context modes.</p></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/guides/python-sdk\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M8 4h5a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v3H9a3 3 0 0 0-3 3v1H4V9a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h5\"></path><path d=\"M16 20h-5a3 3 0 0 1-3-3v-3h7a3 3 0 0 0 3-3v-1h2v5a3 3 0 0 1-3 3h-5\"></path><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"7\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".7\" stroke=\"none\"></circle><circle cx=\"15\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".7\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Embed the Python SDK</strong><p>Construct graphs inside an application with <code>BCG</code>, <code>BCGMemory</code>, and <code>BCGRunner</code>.</p></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/guides/streaming-server\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect height=\"6\" rx=\"1.5\" width=\"16\" x=\"4\" y=\"4\"></rect><rect height=\"6\" rx=\"1.5\" width=\"16\" x=\"4\" y=\"14\"></rect><path d=\"M8 7h.01M8 17h.01M12 7h5M12 17h5\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Run a graph service</strong><p>Push turns over HTTP and retrieve the latest graph per <code>problem_id</code>.</p></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/guides/live-stream-viewer\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M2.5 12s3.5-6 9.5-6 9.5 6 9.5 6-3.5 6-9.5 6-9.5-6-9.5-6Z\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"2.5\"></circle></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Inspect a live run</strong><p>Replay graph growth, inspect evidence, select subgraphs, and explain the final decision.</p></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a></div><p>Runnable examples are available in <a href=\"#/quickstart\">Quick Start</a>, <a href=\"#/guides/manual-beliefs\">Manual beliefs</a>, <a href=\"#/guides/streaming-server\">Streaming HTTP server</a>, and <a href=\"#/guides/batch-construction\">Batch construction</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"current-project-boundaries\">Current project boundaries</h2>\n<p>BCG currently persists complete run artifacts to files and keeps each active construction session in process memory. The repository does <strong>not</strong> include a production graph-database adapter, a multi-node session coordinator, or a hosted control plane. Deploy those concerns around BCG when your application requires them.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout tip\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M8.5 15.5c-1.2-1-2-2.5-2-4.2a5.5 5.5 0 1 1 11 0c0 1.7-.8 3.2-2 4.2-.8.7-1.1 1.2-1.2 2H9.7c-.1-.8-.4-1.3-1.2-2Z\"></path><path d=\"M9.8 20h4.4M10 17.5h4\"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Tip</strong><p>For the shortest working path, install BCG, run <code>bcg setup</code>, and launch <code>bcg</code>. For framework integration, start with the Python SDK or HTTP server instead.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"Typed graph memory From evidence to belief, then decision Evidence preserves exact provenance. Beliefs turn it into typed propositions, and decisions specialize a belief for an action, judgment, or conclusion. Select an element to inspect its role. 01 · record Evidence Exact provenance not a node · any turn role grounds 02 · node Belief Typed proposition confidence · stance · layer specializes 03 · specialized Decision Action or conclusion a specialized belief Selected element Evidence record Exact provenance with source offsets. Evidence is not a graph node and may come from user, assistant, tool, or function turns. Bash Copy curl -LsSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigai-nlco/belief-context-graph/main/install.sh | sh bcg --version Most agent memory systems are optimized for retrieval: preserving conversation history, finding similar fragments, linking entities, or recording what happened. An agent can retrieve the right passage and still act on the wrong belief. Those systems answer retrieval questions— what is relevant, what is related, and what happened? BCG addresses the next layer: what the agent should believe and whether confidence is sufficient to act. The missing questions are: Should the agent believe this claim? How confident should it be? Which exact evidence supports it? What contradicts or qualifies it? Was it formed in this session or inherited from an earlier one? Is uncertainty high enough to block action? Belief Context Graph ( BCG ) upgrades agent memory from retrieval memory to belief computation memory. It turns an agent trajectory into a graph of beliefs, decisions, evidence, confidence, and typed relations. BCG is agent-independent: use the included terminal Agent, embed the Python SDK, or call the streaming HTTP server from your own runtime. What BCG adds Belief-native memory Store beliefs and decisions as first-class typed nodes rather than anonymous chunks. Deterministic confidence Recompute posterior confidence from an explicit prior, merged evidence, and active graph factors. Exact provenance Link every extracted belief back to character offsets in its source turn. Temporal state Track sessions, turns, event time, merge history, and confidence history. Conflict-aware relations Represent dependency, supplementation, and contradiction explicitly. Auditable execution Inspect prompts, embedding calls, merge decisions, timing, token usage, and graph evolution. The core loop Text Copy conversation turn │ ▼ split or semantic chunk │ ▼ extract beliefs + decisions + evidence │ ▼ initialize confidence │ ▼ merge duplicates before linking │ ▼ create typed relations │ ▼ propagate relation confidence │ ▼ queryable BCG + audit artifacts Note BCG does not replace an agent framework. It supplies graph construction, a typed graph model, context assembly, HTTP endpoints, artifacts, and reference integrations beneath your existing agent loop. Start by use case Try the reference Agent Launch the bundled terminal Agent and switch between Default and BCG context modes. ↗ Embed the Python SDK Construct graphs inside an application with BCG , BCGMemory , and BCGRunner . ↗ Run a graph service Push turns over HTTP and retrieve the latest graph per problem_id . ↗ Inspect a live run Replay graph growth, inspect evidence, select subgraphs, and explain the final decision. ↗ Runnable examples are available in Quick Start , Manual beliefs , Streaming HTTP server , and Batch construction . Current project boundaries BCG currently persists complete run artifacts to files and keeps each active construction session in process memory. The repository does not include a production graph-database adapter, a multi-node session coordinator, or a hosted control plane. Deploy those concerns around BCG when your application requires them. Tip For the shortest working path, install BCG, run bcg setup , and launch bcg . For framework integration, start with the Python SDK or HTTP server instead.","headings":[{"id":"what-bcg-adds","text":"What BCG adds","level":2},{"id":"the-core-loop","text":"The core loop","level":2},{"id":"start-by-use-case","text":"Start by use case","level":2},{"id":"current-project-boundaries","text":"Current project boundaries","level":2}],"icon":"brain"},"concepts":{"slug":"concepts","title":"Core Concepts","description":"The small set of ideas that define BCG's belief-native memory model.","html":"<p>BCG models the <em>state of belief</em> that an agent accumulates while acting. The graph is built from a trajectory, but it is not merely a transcript graph.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-model-at-a-glance\">The model at a glance</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Concept</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Belief</strong></td>\n<td>A proposition the system can retain, query, merge, and score</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Decision</strong></td>\n<td>A belief node whose semantic role is an action or conclusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Evidence</strong></td>\n<td>An exact excerpt and source reference supporting a node</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Confidence</strong></td>\n<td>A deterministic posterior built from explicit components</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Relation</strong></td>\n<td>A directional semantic or confidence-propagating connection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Merge</strong></td>\n<td>Canonicalization of semantically duplicate beliefs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Session</strong></td>\n<td>A temporal boundary grouping related turns in one run</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Context policy</strong></td>\n<td>The rule deciding which raw turns remain and which graph state is injected</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"belief-not-just-text\">Belief, not just text</h2>\n<p>A belief contains the proposition text plus:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>node_type</code>: <code>belief</code> or <code>decision</code></li>\n<li><code>stance</code>: <code>asserted</code>, <code>recalled</code>, <code>judged</code>, or <code>speculated</code></li>\n<li><code>layer</code>: <code>io</code> or <code>reasoning</code></li>\n<li>source role and turn metadata</li>\n<li>exact evidence excerpts</li>\n<li>entities and optional event time</li>\n<li>merge lineage</li>\n<li>current confidence and full confidence history</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This makes the node independently inspectable. Retrieval is only one operation over it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"confidence-is-a-graph-calculation\">Confidence is a graph calculation</h2>\n<p>BCG stores the prior and the two update channels separately:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">confidence = sigmoid(\n  logit(initial_confidence)\n  + evidence_confidence\n  + factor_confidence\n)</code></pre></div>\n<p>The current score can therefore be reproduced from graph fields rather than accepted as an opaque model judgment.</p>\n<h2 id=\"relations-have-different-semantics\">Relations have different semantics</h2>\n<p>The active relation vocabulary is:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>depends_on</code> — the source belief depends on the target; strong target confidence can support the source.</li>\n<li><code>supplements</code> — adds context without confidence propagation.</li>\n<li><code>contradicts</code> — the source conflicts with the target and can reduce target confidence when active.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Legacy names remain readable during compatibility migration: <code>informs</code>, <code>extends</code>, and <code>confirms</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-graph-is-also-an-audit-record\">A graph is also an audit record</h2>\n<p>BCG preserves not only the final nodes and edges but also:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>source offsets</li>\n<li>merge groups and rewiring</li>\n<li>confidence updates</li>\n<li>per-turn snapshots</li>\n<li>engine events</li>\n<li>prompts and embedding calls</li>\n<li>timing and token usage</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"doc-card-grid cols-2\"><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/beliefs-and-decisions\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"6\" r=\"2\"></circle><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"6\" r=\"2\"></circle><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"18\" r=\"2\"></circle><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"18\" r=\"2\"></circle><path d=\"m7 7.5 3 2.5m4 0 3-2.5m-10 9 3-2.5m4 0 3 2.5\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Beliefs &amp; decisions</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/confidence\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 16a8 8 0 1 1 16 0\"></path><path d=\"m12 16 4-5\"></path><path d=\"M7 16h10\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Confidence</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/evidence-and-provenance\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M7 17H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-3c0-4 2-7 6-8v3c-2 .7-3 2-3 4h2v6Zm10 0h-3a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-3c0-4 2-7 6-8v3c-2 .7-3 2-3 4h2v6Z\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Evidence &amp; provenance</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/relations\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"12\" r=\"2.5\"></circle><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"2.5\"></circle><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"2.5\"></circle><path d=\"m7.2 10.9 8.5-3.8M7.2 13.1l8.5 3.8\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Relations</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/merging\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2\"></circle><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2\"></circle><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"19\" r=\"2\"></circle><path d=\"M7 7v3c0 4 5 3 5 7M17 7v3c0 4-5 3-5 7\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Merging</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/sessions-and-time\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8\"></circle><path d=\"M12 7v5l3 2\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Sessions &amp; time</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a></div>\n","text":"BCG models the state of belief that an agent accumulates while acting. The graph is built from a trajectory, but it is not merely a transcript graph. The model at a glance Concept Purpose Belief A proposition the system can retain, query, merge, and score Decision A belief node whose semantic role is an action or conclusion Evidence An exact excerpt and source reference supporting a node Confidence A deterministic posterior built from explicit components Relation A directional semantic or confidence-propagating connection Merge Canonicalization of semantically duplicate beliefs Session A temporal boundary grouping related turns in one run Context policy The rule deciding which raw turns remain and which graph state is injected Belief, not just text A belief contains the proposition text plus: node_type : belief or decision stance : asserted , recalled , judged , or speculated layer : io or reasoning source role and turn metadata exact evidence excerpts entities and optional event time merge lineage current confidence and full confidence history This makes the node independently inspectable. Retrieval is only one operation over it. Confidence is a graph calculation BCG stores the prior and the two update channels separately: text Copy confidence = sigmoid( logit(initial_confidence) + evidence_confidence + factor_confidence ) The current score can therefore be reproduced from graph fields rather than accepted as an opaque model judgment. Relations have different semantics The active relation vocabulary is: depends_on — the source belief depends on the target; strong target confidence can support the source. supplements — adds context without confidence propagation. contradicts — the source conflicts with the target and can reduce target confidence when active. Legacy names remain readable during compatibility migration: informs , extends , and confirms . A graph is also an audit record BCG preserves not only the final nodes and edges but also: source offsets merge groups and rewiring confidence updates per-turn snapshots engine events prompts and embedding calls timing and token usage C Beliefs & decisions ↗ G Confidence ↗ Q Evidence & provenance ↗ S Relations ↗ C Merging ↗ C Sessions & time ↗","headings":[{"id":"the-model-at-a-glance","text":"The model at a glance","level":2},{"id":"belief-not-just-text","text":"Belief, not just text","level":2},{"id":"confidence-is-a-graph-calculation","text":"Confidence is a graph calculation","level":2},{"id":"relations-have-different-semantics","text":"Relations have different semantics","level":2},{"id":"a-graph-is-also-an-audit-record","text":"A graph is also an audit record","level":2}],"icon":"book-open"},"architecture":{"slug":"architecture","title":"Architecture","description":"How trajectories become canonical, confidence-bearing belief graphs.","html":"<p>BCG separates public interfaces from its two core construction engines: <code>bcg.construct.api_based</code> and <code>bcg.construct.light</code>.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"BCG architecture overview\" class=\"arch-diagram\">\n<svg aria-labelledby=\"archTitle archDesc\" role=\"img\" viewbox=\"0 0 1040 560\">\n<title id=\"archTitle\">BCG architecture overview</title>\n<desc id=\"archDesc\">Public interfaces feed BCGRunner or SessionManager, then converge on the selected bcg.construct api_based or light StreamingTrajectorySession, which executes split, extract, confidence, merge, relation, and audit stages.</desc>\n<defs>\n<marker id=\"archArrow\" markerheight=\"7\" markerwidth=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\" refx=\"10\" refy=\"6\" viewbox=\"0 0 12 12\">\n<path class=\"arch-arrowhead\" d=\"M1 1 L11 6 L1 11 Z\"></path>\n</marker>\n</defs>\n<rect class=\"arch-card arch-card-top\" height=\"64\" rx=\"18\" width=\"680\" x=\"180\" y=\"24\"></rect>\n<text class=\"arch-text arch-title\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"520\" y=\"64\">Agent / application / batch file / benchmark adapter</text>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"520\" x2=\"520\" y1=\"88\" y2=\"126\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"520\" x2=\"300\" y1=\"126\" y2=\"126\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"520\" x2=\"740\" y1=\"126\" y2=\"126\"></line>\n<text class=\"arch-label\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"300\" y=\"118\">Python SDK</text>\n<text class=\"arch-label\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"740\" y=\"118\">HTTP / CLI</text>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"300\" x2=\"300\" y1=\"126\" y2=\"152\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"740\" x2=\"740\" y1=\"126\" y2=\"152\"></line>\n<rect class=\"arch-card arch-card-left\" height=\"72\" rx=\"18\" width=\"240\" x=\"180\" y=\"156\"></rect>\n<rect class=\"arch-card arch-card-right\" height=\"72\" rx=\"18\" width=\"240\" x=\"620\" y=\"156\"></rect>\n<text class=\"arch-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"300\" y=\"198\">BCGRunner</text>\n<text class=\"arch-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"740\" y=\"198\">SessionManager</text>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"300\" x2=\"300\" y1=\"228\" y2=\"258\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"740\" x2=\"740\" y1=\"228\" y2=\"258\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"300\" x2=\"520\" y1=\"258\" y2=\"258\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" x1=\"740\" x2=\"520\" y1=\"258\" y2=\"258\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"520\" x2=\"520\" y1=\"258\" y2=\"286\"></line>\n<rect class=\"arch-card arch-card-center\" height=\"78\" rx=\"20\" width=\"400\" x=\"320\" y=\"288\"></rect>\n<text class=\"arch-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"520\" y=\"320\">StreamingTrajectorySession</text><text class=\"arch-subtext\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"520\" y=\"345\">bcg.construct.api_based · bcg.construct.light</text>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"520\" x2=\"520\" y1=\"366\" y2=\"392\"></line>\n<rect class=\"arch-stage\" height=\"50\" rx=\"15\" width=\"128\" x=\"84\" y=\"410\"></rect>\n<rect class=\"arch-stage\" height=\"50\" rx=\"15\" width=\"128\" x=\"236\" y=\"410\"></rect>\n<rect class=\"arch-stage\" height=\"50\" rx=\"15\" width=\"128\" x=\"388\" y=\"410\"></rect>\n<rect class=\"arch-stage\" height=\"50\" rx=\"15\" width=\"128\" x=\"540\" y=\"410\"></rect>\n<rect class=\"arch-stage\" height=\"50\" rx=\"15\" width=\"128\" x=\"692\" y=\"410\"></rect>\n<rect class=\"arch-stage\" height=\"50\" rx=\"15\" width=\"112\" x=\"844\" y=\"410\"></rect>\n<text class=\"arch-stage-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"148\" y=\"440\">split</text>\n<text class=\"arch-stage-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"300\" y=\"440\">extract</text>\n<text class=\"arch-stage-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"452\" y=\"440\">confidence</text>\n<text class=\"arch-stage-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"604\" y=\"440\">merge</text>\n<text class=\"arch-stage-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"756\" y=\"440\">relations</text>\n<text class=\"arch-stage-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"900\" y=\"440\">audit</text>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"212\" x2=\"236\" y1=\"435\" y2=\"435\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"364\" x2=\"388\" y1=\"435\" y2=\"435\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"516\" x2=\"540\" y1=\"435\" y2=\"435\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"668\" x2=\"692\" y1=\"435\" y2=\"435\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"820\" x2=\"844\" y1=\"435\" y2=\"435\"></line>\n<line class=\"arch-link\" marker-end=\"url(#archArrow)\" x1=\"520\" x2=\"520\" y1=\"460\" y2=\"488\"></line>\n<rect class=\"arch-card arch-card-bottom\" height=\"52\" rx=\"16\" width=\"368\" x=\"336\" y=\"492\"></rect>\n<text class=\"arch-text\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"520\" y=\"523\">BCG graph + run artifacts</text>\n</svg>\n<p class=\"arch-caption\">The public entry paths converge on the selected backend session. The core stage implementations live in <code>bcg.construct.api_based</code> and <code>bcg.construct.light</code>; the surrounding SDK, HTTP, and CLI layers select and orchestrate one of them.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"public-layers\">Public layers</h2>\n<h3 id=\"graph-model\">Graph model</h3>\n<p><code>bcg.graph</code> defines the typed Pydantic models:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>BCG</code>, <code>BCGNode</code>, <code>BCGEdge</code></li>\n<li><code>BeliefPayload</code>, <code>BeliefSource</code>, <code>EvidenceExcerpt</code></li>\n<li><code>RelationPayload</code>, <code>RelationActivationCondition</code></li>\n<li><code>ConfidenceHistoryEntry</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"memory-facade\">Memory facade</h3>\n<p><code>BCGMemory</code> offers application-facing operations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>manually observe an already-formed belief</li>\n<li>find matching beliefs</li>\n<li>search current graph text</li>\n<li>assemble task context with conflicts and missing-evidence flags</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"construction-lifecycle\">Construction lifecycle</h3>\n<p>BCGRunner owns one run at a time, selects either <code>bcg.construct.api_based</code> or <code>bcg.construct.light</code>, synchronizes snapshots into the public <code>BCG</code> model, tracks sessions, and writes compatibility artifacts. The split, extraction, confidence, merge, and relation logic remains inside the selected <code>bcg.construct</code> package.</p>\n<h3 id=\"cli-and-http\">CLI and HTTP</h3>\n<p>The <code>bcg construct</code> command family wraps the same construction backends for batch, server, replay, and visualization workflows.</p>\n<h2 id=\"incremental-construction-pipeline\">Incremental construction pipeline</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps-list\"><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">1</span><div><h3 id=\"segment-the-turn\">Segment the turn</h3><p><code>api_based</code> uses sentence-oriented evidence or free excerpts. <code>light</code> can use semantic breakpoint chunking and isolates tool calls.</p></div></li><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">2</span><div><h3 id=\"extract-nodes\">Extract nodes</h3><p>The backend produces zero or more belief and decision candidates for the current turn.</p></div></li><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">3</span><div><h3 id=\"initialize-confidence\">Initialize confidence</h3><p>Source reliability and stance quality determine the prior. Evidence and graph factors remain separate components.</p></div></li><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">4</span><div><h3 id=\"merge-before-linking\">Merge before linking</h3><p>Embedding candidates identify possible duplicates. Optional model verification can accept, reject, and rewrite the surviving canonical node.</p></div></li><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">5</span><div><h3 id=\"generate-relations\">Generate relations</h3><p>Relations are created against canonical nodes, preventing new edges from pointing at nodes removed in the same turn.</p></div></li><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">6</span><div><h3 id=\"propagate-confidence\">Propagate confidence</h3><p>Active <code>depends_on</code> and <code>contradicts</code> edges contribute deterministic factors until convergence limits are reached.</p></div></li><li class=\"step-item\"><span class=\"step-number\">7</span><div><h3 id=\"persist-artifacts\">Persist artifacts</h3><p>The final graph, per-turn snapshots, audit logs, timing, token usage, and merge details are written beneath the run output directory.</p></div></li></ol>\n<h2 id=\"backend-boundary\">Backend boundary</h2>\n<p>The core construction logic is implemented in the sibling packages <code>bcg.construct.api_based</code> and <code>bcg.construct.light</code>. They implement the same graph contract but make different infrastructure tradeoffs:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Area</th>\n<th>api_based</th>\n<th>light</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Node and relation generation</td>\n<td>One OpenAI-compatible chat model</td>\n<td>Small generative model via compatible endpoint</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Embeddings</td>\n<td>Configured embedding endpoint or local provider</td>\n<td>Local sentence-transformers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stance</td>\n<td>Inferred through API pipeline</td>\n<td>Required local four-class classifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NER</td>\n<td>Pipeline extraction</td>\n<td>Local spaCy / rules / Hugging Face options</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tuning surface</td>\n<td>CLI flags and stream options</td>\n<td>Full <code>belief_graph</code> config sections</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>See <a href=\"#/backends/choosing-a-backend\">Choosing a backend</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"concurrency-model\">Concurrency model</h2>\n<p>The HTTP server uses <code>ThreadingHTTPServer</code>. Each <code>problem_id</code> owns a separate session and lock:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>turns for the same problem are processed in arrival order</li>\n<li>different problem IDs can execute concurrently</li>\n<li>batch endpoints fan independent items across a worker pool</li>\n<li><code>POST /release</code> removes a completed session from memory</li>\n</ul>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>This is process-local coordination. A load-balanced multi-process deployment needs sticky routing or an external session coordinator.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"BCG separates public interfaces from its two core construction engines: bcg.construct.api_based and bcg.construct.light . BCG architecture overview Public interfaces feed BCGRunner or SessionManager, then converge on the selected bcg.construct api_based or light StreamingTrajectorySession, which executes split, extract, confidence, merge, relation, and audit stages. Agent / application / batch file / benchmark adapter Python SDK HTTP / CLI BCGRunner SessionManager StreamingTrajectorySession bcg.construct.api_based · bcg.construct.light split extract confidence merge relations audit BCG graph + run artifacts The public entry paths converge on the selected backend session. The core stage implementations live in bcg.construct.api_based and bcg.construct.light ; the surrounding SDK, HTTP, and CLI layers select and orchestrate one of them. Public layers Graph model bcg.graph defines the typed Pydantic models: BCG , BCGNode , BCGEdge BeliefPayload , BeliefSource , EvidenceExcerpt RelationPayload , RelationActivationCondition ConfidenceHistoryEntry Memory facade BCGMemory offers application-facing operations: manually observe an already-formed belief find matching beliefs search current graph text assemble task context with conflicts and missing-evidence flags Construction lifecycle BCGRunner owns one run at a time, selects either bcg.construct.api_based or bcg.construct.light , synchronizes snapshots into the public BCG model, tracks sessions, and writes compatibility artifacts. The split, extraction, confidence, merge, and relation logic remains inside the selected bcg.construct package. CLI and HTTP The bcg construct command family wraps the same construction backends for batch, server, replay, and visualization workflows. Incremental construction pipeline 1 Segment the turn api_based uses sentence-oriented evidence or free excerpts. light can use semantic breakpoint chunking and isolates tool calls. 2 Extract nodes The backend produces zero or more belief and decision candidates for the current turn. 3 Initialize confidence Source reliability and stance quality determine the prior. Evidence and graph factors remain separate components. 4 Merge before linking Embedding candidates identify possible duplicates. Optional model verification can accept, reject, and rewrite the surviving canonical node. 5 Generate relations Relations are created against canonical nodes, preventing new edges from pointing at nodes removed in the same turn. 6 Propagate confidence Active depends_on and contradicts edges contribute deterministic factors until convergence limits are reached. 7 Persist artifacts The final graph, per-turn snapshots, audit logs, timing, token usage, and merge details are written beneath the run output directory. Backend boundary The core construction logic is implemented in the sibling packages bcg.construct.api_based and bcg.construct.light . They implement the same graph contract but make different infrastructure tradeoffs: Area api_based light Node and relation generation One OpenAI-compatible chat model Small generative model via compatible endpoint Embeddings Configured embedding endpoint or local provider Local sentence-transformers Stance Inferred through API pipeline Required local four-class classifier NER Pipeline extraction Local spaCy / rules / Hugging Face options Tuning surface CLI flags and stream options Full belief_graph config sections See Choosing a backend . Concurrency model The HTTP server uses ThreadingHTTPServer . Each problem_id owns a separate session and lock: turns for the same problem are processed in arrival order different problem IDs can execute concurrently batch endpoints fan independent items across a worker pool POST /release removes a completed session from memory Warning This is process-local coordination. A load-balanced multi-process deployment needs sticky routing or an external session coordinator.","headings":[{"id":"public-layers","text":"Public layers","level":2},{"id":"graph-model","text":"Graph model","level":3},{"id":"memory-facade","text":"Memory facade","level":3},{"id":"construction-lifecycle","text":"Construction lifecycle","level":3},{"id":"cli-and-http","text":"CLI and HTTP","level":3},{"id":"incremental-construction-pipeline","text":"Incremental construction pipeline","level":2},{"id":"segment-the-turn","text":"Segment the turn","level":3},{"id":"extract-nodes","text":"Extract nodes","level":3},{"id":"initialize-confidence","text":"Initialize confidence","level":3},{"id":"merge-before-linking","text":"Merge before linking","level":3},{"id":"generate-relations","text":"Generate relations","level":3},{"id":"propagate-confidence","text":"Propagate confidence","level":3},{"id":"persist-artifacts","text":"Persist artifacts","level":3},{"id":"backend-boundary","text":"Backend boundary","level":2},{"id":"concurrency-model","text":"Concurrency model","level":2}],"icon":"diagram-project"},"choose-your-path":{"slug":"choose-your-path","title":"Choose Your Path","description":"Select the BCG interface that matches your application.","html":"<p>BCG exposes several entry points over the same belief graph model.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>You need to…</th>\n<th>Start with</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Experience BCG interactively</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/reference-agent\">Reference Agent</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Add graph construction to Python</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/python-sdk\">Python SDK</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Send turns from another language</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/streaming-server\">Streaming HTTP server</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Process saved trajectories or datasets</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/batch-construction\">Batch construction</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reprocess an NDJSON stream</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/replay-streams\">Replay streams</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Inspect graph growth and evidence</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/live-stream-viewer\">Live Stream Viewer</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Compare BCG against raw context</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/benchmarking\">Benchmarking</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Insert known beliefs without an LLM</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/guides/manual-beliefs\">Manual beliefs</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"decision-guide\">Decision guide</h2>\n<div class=\"accordion-group\"><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>I already have an agent framework<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Use the Python SDK when your runtime is Python. Otherwise run <code>bcg construct server</code> and push messages over <code>/turn</code> or <code>/turns</code>. Keep your own tools, UI, model routing, and agent loop.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>I want BCG to manage a reference experience<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Run <code>bcg setup</code>, choose a graph backend, and then launch <code>bcg</code>. The included Agent demonstrates the BCG context policy but is not required.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>I only need to inspect completed output<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Run <code>bcg construct visualize path/to/result.json</code>, or open the live viewer and select an output directory.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>I already have structured beliefs<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Use <code>BCGMemory.observe()</code>. It inserts the full supplied content as one asserted belief and performs no model call.</p></div></details></div>\n","text":"BCG exposes several entry points over the same belief graph model. You need to… Start with Experience BCG interactively Reference Agent Add graph construction to Python Python SDK Send turns from another language Streaming HTTP server Process saved trajectories or datasets Batch construction Reprocess an NDJSON stream Replay streams Inspect graph growth and evidence Live Stream Viewer Compare BCG against raw context Benchmarking Insert known beliefs without an LLM Manual beliefs Decision guide I already have an agent framework + Use the Python SDK when your runtime is Python. Otherwise run bcg construct server and push messages over /turn or /turns . Keep your own tools, UI, model routing, and agent loop. I want BCG to manage a reference experience + Run bcg setup , choose a graph backend, and then launch bcg . The included Agent demonstrates the BCG context policy but is not required. I only need to inspect completed output + Run bcg construct visualize path/to/result.json , or open the live viewer and select an output directory. I already have structured beliefs + Use BCGMemory.observe() . It inserts the full supplied content as one asserted belief and performs no model call.","headings":[{"id":"decision-guide","text":"Decision guide","level":2}],"icon":"route"},"glossary":{"slug":"glossary","title":"Glossary","description":"Terms used throughout the BCG codebase and documentation.","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Belief</strong></td>\n<td>A proposition represented as a typed graph node</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Decision</strong></td>\n<td>A node marked <code>node_type=\"decision\"</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Trajectory</strong></td>\n<td>Ordered messages supplied to graph construction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Turn</strong></td>\n<td>One trajectory message or a fully assembled streamed message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Segment</strong></td>\n<td>A sentence, semantic chunk, or isolated tool-call unit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Evidence</strong></td>\n<td>Source text excerpt with optional exact offsets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Stance</strong></td>\n<td><code>asserted</code>, <code>recalled</code>, <code>judged</code>, or <code>speculated</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Layer</strong></td>\n<td><code>io</code> for user/tool-facing content, <code>reasoning</code> for assistant reasoning</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Prior</strong></td>\n<td><code>initial_confidence</code>, derived from source reliability and stance quality</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Evidence contribution</strong></td>\n<td><code>evidence_confidence</code>, updated as evidence accumulates</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Factor contribution</strong></td>\n<td><code>factor_confidence</code>, propagated through active relations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Canonical node</strong></td>\n<td>The surviving node after a merge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Merge verification</strong></td>\n<td>Optional model gate and rewrite for embedding-proposed duplicates</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Activation condition</strong></td>\n<td>Minimum confidence required before an edge propagates a factor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Snapshot</strong></td>\n<td>Graph state emitted after a turn or finalization</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Run</strong></td>\n<td>One construction lifecycle with a stable <code>run_id</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Session</strong></td>\n<td>A logical temporal group of turns inside a run</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Problem ID</strong></td>\n<td>HTTP streaming key selecting one active graph session</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>BCG context mode</strong></td>\n<td>Reference Agent policy that retains a small raw window and injects graph memory</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","text":"Term Meaning Belief A proposition represented as a typed graph node Decision A node marked node_type=\"decision\" Trajectory Ordered messages supplied to graph construction Turn One trajectory message or a fully assembled streamed message Segment A sentence, semantic chunk, or isolated tool-call unit Evidence Source text excerpt with optional exact offsets Stance asserted , recalled , judged , or speculated Layer io for user/tool-facing content, reasoning for assistant reasoning Prior initial_confidence , derived from source reliability and stance quality Evidence contribution evidence_confidence , updated as evidence accumulates Factor contribution factor_confidence , propagated through active relations Canonical node The surviving node after a merge Merge verification Optional model gate and rewrite for embedding-proposed duplicates Activation condition Minimum confidence required before an edge propagates a factor Snapshot Graph state emitted after a turn or finalization Run One construction lifecycle with a stable run_id Session A logical temporal group of turns inside a run Problem ID HTTP streaming key selecting one active graph session BCG context mode Reference Agent policy that retains a small raw window and injects graph memory","headings":[],"icon":"list"},"concepts/beliefs-and-decisions":{"slug":"concepts/beliefs-and-decisions","title":"Beliefs & Decisions","description":"The typed nodes that carry BCG's memory state.","html":"<p>A BCG node wraps a <code>BeliefPayload</code>. The payload is the stable application-level record; the outer <code>BCGNode</code> supplies a UUID, timestamps, generic kind, and extension payload.</p>\n<h2 id=\"belief-payload\">Belief payload</h2>\n<p>Important fields include:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Field</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>id</code></td>\n<td>Monotonic integer identifier within the graph</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>node_type</code></td>\n<td><code>belief</code> or <code>decision</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>belief</code></td>\n<td>Canonical proposition text</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>decision</code></td>\n<td>Optional decision-specific text</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>stance</code></td>\n<td><code>asserted</code>, <code>recalled</code>, <code>judged</code>, or <code>speculated</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>layer</code></td>\n<td><code>io</code> or <code>reasoning</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>role</code></td>\n<td>Source message role</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>entities</code></td>\n<td>Extracted entity labels</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>source</code></td>\n<td>Turn, segment, session, and scenario provenance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>evidence_ids</code></td>\n<td>References into graph-level evidence records</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>factor_ids</code></td>\n<td>References into factor records</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>merged_from</code></td>\n<td>IDs absorbed into this canonical node</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>confidence</code></td>\n<td>Current posterior</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>confidence_history</code></td>\n<td>Reproducible update audit</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"belief-vs-decision\">Belief vs decision</h2>\n<p>A decision is represented by the same core payload with:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"node_type\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"decision\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"belief\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Prioritize a reliability review for Acme.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"decision\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Prioritize a reliability review for Acme.\"</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>This keeps decisions connected to the same evidence, confidence, relation, and temporal machinery as other beliefs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"stance\">Stance</h2>\n<p>Stance captures how the speaker presents a proposition:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Stance</th>\n<th>Typical language</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>asserted</code></td>\n<td>“The service is down.”</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>recalled</code></td>\n<td>“I remember the service failed last week.”</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>judged</code></td>\n<td>“This pattern suggests a capacity issue.”</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>speculated</code></td>\n<td>“The database might be overloaded.”</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Stance contributes to the prior. It is not a truth label.</p>\n<h2 id=\"layers\">Layers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>io</code> usually holds externally visible interaction state and propositions grounded in turns, tool outputs, or function I/O.</li>\n<li><code>reasoning</code> usually holds latent reasoning-layer propositions, model-side synthesis, and decision-oriented summaries.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The layer is useful for filtering context and auditing how an output was derived from inputs. It is orthogonal to node type and provenance: decisions are a specialized kind of belief node, and evidence excerpts can be attached regardless of whether the host turn came from a user, assistant, tool, or function.</p>\n","text":"A BCG node wraps a BeliefPayload . The payload is the stable application-level record; the outer BCGNode supplies a UUID, timestamps, generic kind, and extension payload. Belief payload Important fields include: Field Meaning id Monotonic integer identifier within the graph node_type belief or decision belief Canonical proposition text decision Optional decision-specific text stance asserted , recalled , judged , or speculated layer io or reasoning role Source message role entities Extracted entity labels source Turn, segment, session, and scenario provenance evidence_ids References into graph-level evidence records factor_ids References into factor records merged_from IDs absorbed into this canonical node confidence Current posterior confidence_history Reproducible update audit Belief vs decision A decision is represented by the same core payload with: json Copy { \"node_type\": \"decision\", \"belief\": \"Prioritize a reliability review for Acme.\", \"decision\": \"Prioritize a reliability review for Acme.\" } This keeps decisions connected to the same evidence, confidence, relation, and temporal machinery as other beliefs. Stance Stance captures how the speaker presents a proposition: Stance Typical language asserted “The service is down.” recalled “I remember the service failed last week.” judged “This pattern suggests a capacity issue.” speculated “The database might be overloaded.” Stance contributes to the prior. It is not a truth label. Layers io generally contains user, tool, and function-facing beliefs. reasoning generally contains assistant reasoning and decisions. The layer is useful for filtering context and auditing how an output was derived from inputs.","headings":[{"id":"belief-payload","text":"Belief payload","level":2},{"id":"belief-vs-decision","text":"Belief vs decision","level":2},{"id":"stance","text":"Stance","level":2},{"id":"layers","text":"Layers","level":2}],"icon":"brain"},"concepts/confidence":{"slug":"concepts/confidence","title":"Confidence","description":"How BCG computes an auditable posterior for every belief.","html":"<p>BCG confidence is represented as explicit components rather than a single unexplained score.</p>\n<h2 id=\"posterior-formula\">Posterior formula</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">confidence = sigmoid(\n  logit(initial_confidence)\n  + evidence_confidence\n  + factor_confidence\n)</code></pre></div>\n<p>Scores are clamped away from exact zero and one before logit conversion.</p>\n<h2 id=\"components\">Components</h2>\n<h3 id=\"initial-confidence\">Initial confidence</h3>\n<p>The prior is derived from:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>source reliability</li>\n<li>stance quality</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The default configuration uses a weighted average of the two. Example policy values assign higher reliability to tool results than to LLM reasoning, and lower stance quality to speculation than to assertion.</p>\n<h3 id=\"evidence-confidence\">Evidence confidence</h3>\n<p>This component changes as evidence is attached or merged. Evidence remains separately inspectable through <code>evidence_ids</code>, excerpt text, and source offsets.</p>\n<h3 id=\"factor-confidence\">Factor confidence</h3>\n<p>This component is produced by active graph relations. It records how supporting dependencies or contradictions changed the target posterior.</p>\n<h2 id=\"confidence-history\">Confidence history</h2>\n<p>Each update may record:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>step and resulting value</li>\n<li>reason and delta</li>\n<li>confidence configuration</li>\n<li>iteration</li>\n<li>evidence added or scored</li>\n<li>absorbed beliefs</li>\n<li>factor details</li>\n<li>formula and method</li>\n<li>fallback use</li>\n<li>model name</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">entry</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">confidence_history</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">model_dump</span><span class=\"p\">())</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"relation-activation\">Relation activation</h2>\n<p>Confidence-carrying edges can have:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"weight\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"activated_condition\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"input_conf_threshold\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.8</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The relation only contributes after the relevant input belief crosses the threshold.</p>\n<h2 id=\"propagation-semantics\">Propagation semantics</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>depends_on</code>: positive support flows from <code>to_id</code> to <code>from_id</code></li>\n<li><code>contradicts</code>: negative support flows from <code>from_id</code> to <code>to_id</code></li>\n<li><code>supplements</code>: semantic-only; no confidence weight or activation condition</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The configuration limits minimum deltas and propagation iterations.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>Confidence is a policy-controlled graph score, not a calibrated probability guarantee. Validate the policy for your domain before using it as an action threshold.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"BCG confidence is represented as explicit components rather than a single unexplained score. Posterior formula text Copy confidence = sigmoid( logit(initial_confidence) + evidence_confidence + factor_confidence ) Scores are clamped away from exact zero and one before logit conversion. Components Initial confidence The prior is derived from: source reliability stance quality The default configuration uses a weighted average of the two. Example policy values assign higher reliability to tool results than to LLM reasoning, and lower stance quality to speculation than to assertion. Evidence confidence This component changes as evidence is attached or merged. Evidence remains separately inspectable through evidence_ids , excerpt text, and source offsets. Factor confidence This component is produced by active graph relations. It records how supporting dependencies or contradictions changed the target posterior. Confidence history Each update may record: step and resulting value reason and delta confidence configuration iteration evidence added or scored absorbed beliefs factor details formula and method fallback use model name python Copy for entry in belief.confidence_history: print(entry.model_dump()) Relation activation Confidence-carrying edges can have: json Copy { \"weight\": 0.7, \"activated_condition\": { \"input_conf_threshold\": 0.8 } } The relation only contributes after the relevant input belief crosses the threshold. Propagation semantics depends_on : positive support flows from to_id to from_id contradicts : negative support flows from from_id to to_id supplements : semantic-only; no confidence weight or activation condition The configuration limits minimum deltas and propagation iterations. W Warning Confidence is a policy-controlled graph score, not a calibrated probability guarantee. Validate the policy for your domain before using it as an action threshold.","headings":[{"id":"posterior-formula","text":"Posterior formula","level":2},{"id":"components","text":"Components","level":2},{"id":"initial-confidence","text":"Initial confidence","level":3},{"id":"evidence-confidence","text":"Evidence confidence","level":3},{"id":"factor-confidence","text":"Factor confidence","level":3},{"id":"confidence-history","text":"Confidence history","level":2},{"id":"relation-activation","text":"Relation activation","level":2},{"id":"propagation-semantics","text":"Propagation semantics","level":2}],"icon":"gauge-high"},"concepts/evidence-and-provenance":{"slug":"concepts/evidence-and-provenance","title":"Evidence & Provenance","description":"Trace a belief back to the exact text that produced it.","html":"<p>Evidence is stored both as graph-level records and as typed excerpts attached to belief payloads.</p>\n<h2 id=\"evidence-excerpt\">Evidence excerpt</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">EvidenceExcerpt</span>\n<span class=\"n\">excerpt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">EvidenceExcerpt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Acme is threatening to churn\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">start</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">end</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">29</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">match</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"exact\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">via</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"split_sentence\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">belief_source</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Supported provenance fields include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>excerpt <code>text</code></li>\n<li>start and exclusive end offsets</li>\n<li>match quality: <code>exact</code>, <code>normalized</code>, <code>fuzzy</code>, or <code>not_found</code></li>\n<li>extraction path: <code>llm_excerpt</code>, <code>split_sentence</code>, <code>semantic_chunk</code>, or <code>manual</code></li>\n<li>role, trajectory index, segment index, session, and turn metadata</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"evidence-modes\">Evidence modes</h2>\n<div class=\"offline-tabs\"><div class=\"tab-list\"><button class=\"tab-button active\" data-tab-index=\"0\" type=\"button\">Sentence</button><button class=\"tab-button\" data-tab-index=\"1\" type=\"button\">Excerpt</button><button class=\"tab-button\" data-tab-index=\"2\" type=\"button\">Semantic chunk</button></div><section class=\"tab-panel active\" data-tab-panel=\"0\"><p>The <code>api_based</code> backend uses whole-sentence evidence with offsets. This is the CLI default.</p></section><section class=\"tab-panel\" data-tab-panel=\"1\"><p>The model quotes a free span verbatim. Use:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>trajectory.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--evidence-mode<span class=\"w\"> </span>excerpt</code></pre></div></section><section class=\"tab-panel\" data-tab-panel=\"2\"><p>The <code>light</code> backend can use embedding-distance semantic chunks and isolate tool calls before extraction.</p></section></div>\n<h2 id=\"why-offsets-matter\">Why offsets matter</h2>\n<p>Exact offsets enable:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>evidence highlighting in the viewer</li>\n<li>reproducible review against the original turn</li>\n<li>detection of unsupported summaries</li>\n<li>human correction without rereading the full trajectory</li>\n<li>audit records that survive node rewrites during merge</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The live viewer renders evidence with a warm yellow highlight and links it to the corresponding graph node.</p>\n<h2 id=\"missing-evidence\">Missing evidence</h2>\n<p><code>BCGMemory.context()</code> and <code>search()</code> can retain nodes with missing-evidence flags when <code>include_missing_evidence=True</code>. This helps applications distinguish a semantically relevant node from a well-supported one.</p>\n","text":"Evidence is stored both as graph-level records and as typed excerpts attached to belief payloads. Evidence excerpt python Copy from bcg.graph import EvidenceExcerpt excerpt = EvidenceExcerpt( text=\"Acme is threatening to churn\", start=0, end=29, match=\"exact\", via=\"split_sentence\", source=belief_source, ) Supported provenance fields include: excerpt text start and exclusive end offsets match quality: exact , normalized , fuzzy , or not_found extraction path: llm_excerpt , split_sentence , semantic_chunk , or manual role, trajectory index, segment index, session, and turn metadata Evidence modes Sentence Excerpt Semantic chunk The api_based backend uses whole-sentence evidence with offsets. This is the CLI default. The model quotes a free span verbatim. Use: bash Copy text Copy bcg construct run api_based \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --evidence-mode excerpt The light backend can use embedding-distance semantic chunks and isolate tool calls before extraction. Why offsets matter Exact offsets enable: evidence highlighting in the viewer reproducible review against the original turn detection of unsupported summaries human correction without rereading the full trajectory audit records that survive node rewrites during merge The live viewer renders evidence with a warm yellow highlight and links it to the corresponding graph node. Missing evidence BCGMemory.context() and search() can retain nodes with missing-evidence flags when include_missing_evidence=True . This helps applications distinguish a semantically relevant node from a well-supported one.","headings":[{"id":"evidence-excerpt","text":"Evidence excerpt","level":2},{"id":"evidence-modes","text":"Evidence modes","level":2},{"id":"why-offsets-matter","text":"Why offsets matter","level":2},{"id":"missing-evidence","text":"Missing evidence","level":2}],"icon":"highlighter"},"concepts/relations":{"slug":"concepts/relations","title":"Relations","description":"Directional edges for dependency, supplementation, and contradiction.","html":"<p>A relation connects belief IDs and may carry confidence propagation policy.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">RelationPayload</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relation</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">RelationPayload</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">from_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">to_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">type</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"depends_on\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">note</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"The recommended action depends on the recurring outage claim.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">weight</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"active-relation-types\">Active relation types</h2>\n<h3 id=\"depends-on\"><code>depends_on</code></h3>\n<p>The source belief relies on the target belief.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">decision: contact Acme urgently\n              │ depends_on\n              ▼\nbelief: outages are recurring</code></pre></div>\n<p>Support propagates from <code>to_id</code> to <code>from_id</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"supplements\"><code>supplements</code></h3>\n<p>The target adds useful context but is not a confidence factor. The current construction policy keeps <code>weight</code> and <code>activated_condition</code> as <code>null</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"contradicts\"><code>contradicts</code></h3>\n<p>The source conflicts with the target. When active, confidence can be reduced in the configured direction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"compatibility-names\">Compatibility names</h2>\n<p>The public schema can still read:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Legacy</th>\n<th>Current semantic equivalent</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>informs</code></td>\n<td><code>depends_on</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>extends</code></td>\n<td><code>supplements</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>confirms</code></td>\n<td>supportive legacy relation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The live viewer may display legacy supportive edges as <code>supports</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"graph-integrity\">Graph integrity</h2>\n<p><code>BCG</code> validates relation endpoints against active belief IDs. During a merge, <code>remap_relations()</code> rewrites endpoints and drops invalid or duplicate edges.</p>\n","text":"A relation connects belief IDs and may carry confidence propagation policy. python Copy from bcg.graph import RelationPayload relation = RelationPayload( from_id=3, to_id=1, type=\"depends_on\", note=\"The recommended action depends on the recurring outage claim.\", weight=0.7, ) Active relation types depends_on The source belief relies on the target belief. text Copy decision: contact Acme urgently │ depends_on ▼ belief: outages are recurring Support propagates from to_id to from_id . supplements The target adds useful context but is not a confidence factor. The current construction policy keeps weight and activated_condition as null . contradicts The source conflicts with the target. When active, confidence can be reduced in the configured direction. Compatibility names The public schema can still read: Legacy Current semantic equivalent informs depends_on extends supplements confirms supportive legacy relation The live viewer may display legacy supportive edges as supports . Graph integrity BCG validates relation endpoints against active belief IDs. During a merge, remap_relations() rewrites endpoints and drops invalid or duplicate edges.","headings":[{"id":"active-relation-types","text":"Active relation types","level":2},{"id":"depends-on","text":"depends_on","level":3},{"id":"supplements","text":"supplements","level":3},{"id":"contradicts","text":"contradicts","level":3},{"id":"compatibility-names","text":"Compatibility names","level":2},{"id":"graph-integrity","text":"Graph integrity","level":2}],"icon":"share-nodes"},"concepts/merging":{"slug":"concepts/merging","title":"Merging","description":"How BCG converts repeated observations into canonical beliefs.","html":"<p>Agents often restate the same proposition across turns. BCG merges duplicates before relation generation so the graph does not fragment into near-identical nodes.</p>\n<h2 id=\"merge-order\">Merge order</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">new candidates\n    │\n    ▼\nembedding similarity\n    │\n    ▼\noptional LLM verify + rewrite\n    │\n    ▼\nselect canonical node\n    │\n    ▼\ncombine evidence and lineage\n    │\n    ▼\nrewire existing relations\n    │\n    ▼\ngenerate new relations</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"incremental-merge-controls\">Incremental merge controls</h2>\n<p>For <code>api_based</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>trajectory.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--incremental-merge<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--incremental-merge-threshold<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.86<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--verify-merge</code></pre></div>\n<p>Disable candidate merging:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>trajectory.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--no-incremental-merge</code></pre></div>\n<p>The library defaults differ from some CLI defaults. <code>BCGRunner</code> defaults to threshold <code>0.8</code> and <code>verify_merge=False</code>; the batch and server command layers use their own values.</p>\n<h2 id=\"audit-trail\">Audit trail</h2>\n<p>Merge artifacts record:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>candidate groups</li>\n<li>similarity values</li>\n<li>optional model verification</li>\n<li>accepted and rejected merges</li>\n<li>canonical text rewrites</li>\n<li>absorbed belief IDs</li>\n<li>edge rewiring</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Canonical nodes retain <code>merged_from</code> and may preserve <code>belief_original</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"design-tradeoff\">Design tradeoff</h2>\n<p>A lower threshold creates a smaller graph but risks collapsing distinct propositions. A higher threshold preserves nuance but may create redundant context. Evaluate both node quality and downstream relation quality.</p>\n","text":"Agents often restate the same proposition across turns. BCG merges duplicates before relation generation so the graph does not fragment into near-identical nodes. Merge order text Copy new candidates │ ▼ embedding similarity │ ▼ optional LLM verify + rewrite │ ▼ select canonical node │ ▼ combine evidence and lineage │ ▼ rewire existing relations │ ▼ generate new relations Incremental merge controls For api_based : bash Copy bcg construct run api_based \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --incremental-merge \\ --incremental-merge-threshold 0.86 \\ --verify-merge Disable candidate merging: bash Copy bcg construct run api_based \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --no-incremental-merge The library defaults differ from some CLI defaults. BCGRunner defaults to threshold 0.8 and verify_merge=False ; the batch and server command layers use their own values. Audit trail Merge artifacts record: candidate groups similarity values optional model verification accepted and rejected merges canonical text rewrites absorbed belief IDs edge rewiring Canonical nodes retain merged_from and may preserve belief_original . Design tradeoff A lower threshold creates a smaller graph but risks collapsing distinct propositions. A higher threshold preserves nuance but may create redundant context. Evaluate both node quality and downstream relation quality.","headings":[{"id":"merge-order","text":"Merge order","level":2},{"id":"incremental-merge-controls","text":"Incremental merge controls","level":2},{"id":"audit-trail","text":"Audit trail","level":2},{"id":"design-tradeoff","text":"Design tradeoff","level":2}],"icon":"code-merge"},"concepts/sessions-and-time":{"slug":"concepts/sessions-and-time","title":"Sessions & Time","description":"Temporal boundaries and source metadata inside one belief run.","html":"<p>BCG provides run-based lifecycle and explicit session metadata.</p>\n<h2 id=\"run\">Run</h2>\n<p>A run has:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>stable <code>run_id</code></li>\n<li>scenario and item ID</li>\n<li>one selected construction backend</li>\n<li>trajectory and session list</li>\n<li>graph metadata</li>\n<li>output paths and artifacts</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"session\">Session</h2>\n<p>Use explicit sessions when a trajectory spans meetings, days, users, or phases.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">begin_belief_run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">run_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"customer-history\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start_session</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"support-call-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2026-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;06-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;12\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"The outage happened again.\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"I will escalate the reliability review.\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">end_session</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finalize</span><span class=\"p\">()</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Each observed turn records:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>session_id</code></li>\n<li><code>session_index</code></li>\n<li>session date</li>\n<li>turn index</li>\n<li>optional <code>has_answer</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you call <code>observe_turn()</code> without an active session, <code>BCGRunner</code> creates one automatically.</p>\n<h2 id=\"event-time-vs-observation-time\">Event time vs observation time</h2>\n<p>A belief can carry:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>source session and turn time</li>\n<li><code>event_time</code> for when the described event occurred</li>\n<li><code>time_text</code> preserving the original temporal expression</li>\n<li>node <code>created_at</code> and <code>updated_at</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>These are different concepts. “The outage happened last Tuesday” is observed now but describes an earlier event.</p>\n<h2 id=\"current-persistence-model\">Current persistence model</h2>\n<p>Sessions are serialized in graph artifacts. Active HTTP sessions remain in process memory until finalization and optional release.</p>\n","text":"BCG provides run-based lifecycle and explicit session metadata. Run A run has: stable run_id scenario and item ID one selected construction backend trajectory and session list graph metadata output paths and artifacts Session Use explicit sessions when a trajectory spans meetings, days, users, or phases. python Copy runner.begin_belief_run(run_id=\"customer-history\") runner.start_session(\"support-call-1\", \"2026-06-12\") await runner.observe_turn(\"user\", \"The outage happened again.\") await runner.observe_turn(\"assistant\", \"I will escalate the reliability review.\") await runner.end_session() result = await runner.finalize() Each observed turn records: session_id session_index session date turn index optional has_answer If you call observe_turn() without an active session, BCGRunner creates one automatically. Event time vs observation time A belief can carry: source session and turn time event_time for when the described event occurred time_text preserving the original temporal expression node created_at and updated_at These are different concepts. “The outage happened last Tuesday” is observed now but describes an earlier event. Current persistence model Sessions are serialized in graph artifacts. Active HTTP sessions remain in process memory until finalization and optional release.","headings":[{"id":"run","text":"Run","level":2},{"id":"session","text":"Session","level":2},{"id":"event-time-vs-observation-time","text":"Event time vs observation time","level":2},{"id":"current-persistence-model","text":"Current persistence model","level":2}],"icon":"clock-rotate-left"},"concepts/context-policy":{"slug":"concepts/context-policy","title":"Context Policy","description":"How the reference Agent combines recent raw turns with graph memory.","html":"<p>Graph construction is only half of memory. An agent also needs a policy for deciding what enters the next model request.</p>\n<h2 id=\"reference-bcg-policy\">Reference BCG policy</h2>\n<p>The included Agent:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>retains the initial user input permanently</li>\n<li>retains the latest two completed turns as raw messages</li>\n<li>sends older evicted messages to Graph Construction</li>\n<li>injects the current graph as Markdown into the system prompt</li>\n<li>disables conventional conversation compaction</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-xml\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>XML</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"xml\"><span class=\"nt\">&lt;belief_graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"na\">format=</span><span class=\"s\">\"markdown\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;</span>\n#<span class=\"w\"> </span>Beliefs\n...\n<span class=\"nt\">&lt;/belief_graph&gt;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>This policy gives the model:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>exact recent interaction text</li>\n<li>stable task intent</li>\n<li>compressed long-horizon belief state</li>\n<li>confidence and contradiction signals</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"why-a-hybrid-window\">Why a hybrid window</h2>\n<p>Keeping only graph state can lose phrasing, formatting, or immediate conversational intent. Keeping all raw turns makes context cost grow without bound. A small raw window plus structured graph memory balances the two.</p>\n<h2 id=\"customize-the-window\">Customize the window</h2>\n<p>For the reference Agent:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\"><span class=\"nb\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">BCG_RECENT_TURNS</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;4\nbcg</code></pre></div>\n<p>For a custom agent, choose the window and graph rendering yourself.</p>\n<h2 id=\"integration-questions\">Integration questions</h2>\n<p>Before adopting a policy, decide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Which roles are safe to convert to graph memory?</li>\n<li>Should tool outputs remain verbatim longer than assistant reasoning?</li>\n<li>Which belief confidence is required for prompt injection?</li>\n<li>Should contradictions be included or resolved first?</li>\n<li>How much graph text fits the model context?</li>\n<li>Which nodes must remain hidden from a user-facing response?</li>\n</ul>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>BCG supplies graph state and provenance. Your application remains responsible for authorization, prompt construction, data minimization, and action gating.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"Graph construction is only half of memory. An agent also needs a policy for deciding what enters the next model request. Reference BCG policy The included Agent: retains the initial user input permanently retains the latest two completed turns as raw messages sends older evicted messages to Graph Construction injects the current graph as Markdown into the system prompt disables conventional conversation compaction xml Copy <belief_graph format=\"markdown\"> # Beliefs ... </belief_graph> This policy gives the model: exact recent interaction text stable task intent compressed long-horizon belief state confidence and contradiction signals Why a hybrid window Keeping only graph state can lose phrasing, formatting, or immediate conversational intent. Keeping all raw turns makes context cost grow without bound. A small raw window plus structured graph memory balances the two. Customize the window For the reference Agent: bash Copy export BCG_RECENT_TURNS=4 bcg For a custom agent, choose the window and graph rendering yourself. Integration questions Before adopting a policy, decide: Which roles are safe to convert to graph memory? Should tool outputs remain verbatim longer than assistant reasoning? Which belief confidence is required for prompt injection? Should contradictions be included or resolved first? How much graph text fits the model context? Which nodes must remain hidden from a user-facing response? W Warning BCG supplies graph state and provenance. Your application remains responsible for authorization, prompt construction, data minimization, and action gating.","headings":[{"id":"reference-bcg-policy","text":"Reference BCG policy","level":2},{"id":"why-a-hybrid-window","text":"Why a hybrid window","level":2},{"id":"customize-the-window","text":"Customize the window","level":2},{"id":"integration-questions","text":"Integration questions","level":2}],"icon":"shield-check"},"installation":{"slug":"installation","title":"Installation","description":"Install the BCG SDK, command line, and optional reference Agent.","html":"<p>BCG requires Python 3.11–3.13. The reference terminal Agent additionally requires Node.js 22.19 or newer.</p>\n<h2 id=\"global-installation\">Global installation</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-LsSf<span class=\"w\"> </span>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigai-nlco/belief-context-graph/main/install.sh<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>sh\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>--version</code></pre></div>\n<p>The installer requires <code>curl</code>, <code>tar</code>, npm, and Node.js. It installs <code>uv</code> when needed, installs the Python package and Node runtime, and removes the temporary checkout.</p>\n<h2 id=\"source-installation\">Source installation</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">git<span class=\"w\"> </span>clone<span class=\"w\"> </span>https://github.com/bigai-nlco/belief-context-graph.git\n<span class=\"nb\">cd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>belief-context-graph\n\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>sync\nnpm<span class=\"w\"> </span>--prefix<span class=\"w\"> </span>agent-cli<span class=\"w\"> </span>ci\nnpm<span class=\"w\"> </span>--prefix<span class=\"w\"> </span>agent-cli<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>build\n\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>--version</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run commands from the checkout with <code>uv run</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">uv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help</code></pre></div>\n<p>To expose this checkout globally:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">uv<span class=\"w\"> </span>tool<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span>--editable<span class=\"w\"> </span>.\nnpm<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span>-g<span class=\"w\"> </span>./agent-cli\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>--version</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"python-sdk-only\">Python SDK only</h2>\n<p>The Python package contains the SDK and graph construction services. The Node runtime is only needed for the bundled terminal Agent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">uv<span class=\"w\"> </span>sync\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>python<span class=\"w\"> </span>-c<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"from bcg import BCG, BCGMemory, BCGRunner; print('ready')\"</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"development-dependencies\">Development dependencies</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">uv<span class=\"w\"> </span>sync<span class=\"w\"> </span>--group<span class=\"w\"> </span>dev\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>pytest\nuv<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>ruff<span class=\"w\"> </span>check<span class=\"w\"> </span>.</code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout info\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M12 10.5v6\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.2\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Info</strong><p>Optional benchmark dependencies are declared under the <code>benchmarks</code> extra.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"BCG requires Python 3.11–3.13. The reference terminal Agent additionally requires Node.js 22.19 or newer. Global installation bash Copy curl -LsSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigai-nlco/belief-context-graph/main/install.sh | sh bcg --version The installer requires curl , tar , npm, and Node.js. It installs uv when needed, installs the Python package and Node runtime, and removes the temporary checkout. Source installation bash Copy git clone https://github.com/bigai-nlco/belief-context-graph.git cd belief-context-graph uv sync npm --prefix agent-cli ci npm --prefix agent-cli run build uv run bcg --version Run commands from the checkout with uv run : bash Copy uv run bcg uv run bcg construct --help To expose this checkout globally: bash Copy uv tool install --editable . npm install -g ./agent-cli bcg --version Python SDK only The Python package contains the SDK and graph construction services. The Node runtime is only needed for the bundled terminal Agent. bash Copy uv sync uv run python -c \"from bcg import BCG, BCGMemory, BCGRunner; print('ready')\" Development dependencies bash Copy uv sync --group dev uv run pytest uv run ruff check . I Info Optional benchmark dependencies are declared under the benchmarks extra.","headings":[{"id":"global-installation","text":"Global installation","level":2},{"id":"source-installation","text":"Source installation","level":2},{"id":"python-sdk-only","text":"Python SDK only","level":2},{"id":"development-dependencies","text":"Development dependencies","level":2}],"icon":"download"},"quickstart":{"slug":"quickstart","title":"Quick Start","description":"Build and inspect a belief graph in a few minutes.","html":"<p>This quick start uses the <code>api_based</code> backend through the Python SDK.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-configure-the-model-endpoint\">1. Configure the model endpoint</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\"><span class=\"nb\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">OPENAI_API_KEY</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"...\"</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">OPENAI_BASE_URL</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://api.openai.com/v1\"</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">OPENAI_MODEL</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"gpt-class=\"</span>tok-number<span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;4.1-mini\"</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"2-build-a-graph\">2. Build a graph</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">asyncio</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.llm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"k\">async</span> <span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">memory</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">runner</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">llm</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">backend</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"api_based\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n    <span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_trajectory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">[</span>\n            <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n                <span class=\"s2\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                <span class=\"s2\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"Acme is threatening to churn after repeated outages.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"p\">},</span>\n            <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n                <span class=\"s2\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                <span class=\"s2\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span>\n                    <span class=\"s2\">\"We should prioritize a reliability review and contact Acme. \"</span>\n                    <span class=\"s2\">\"This is urgent because the outages are recurring.\"</span>\n                <span class=\"p\">),</span>\n            <span class=\"p\">},</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">],</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">run_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"acme-risk-review\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"beliefs:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">len</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beliefs</span><span class=\"p\">()))</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"relations:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">len</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">relations</span><span class=\"p\">()))</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"graph:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">output_paths</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"memory:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">output_paths</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">asyncio</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"3-inspect-beliefs-and-context\">3. Inspect beliefs and context</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beliefs</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">node_type</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">confidence</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Decide the next customer-success action\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"4-render-an-html-graph\">4. Render an HTML graph</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>.bcg/runs/acme-risk-review/result.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output<span class=\"w\"> </span>acme-risk-review.html</code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout note\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M6 3h9l4 4v14H6V3Z\"></path><path d=\"M15 3v5h5M9 12h6M9 16h5\"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Note</strong><p><code>observe_trajectory()</code> automatically begins the run, pushes every turn, closes the active session, finalizes the backend, synchronizes the public graph, and writes artifacts.</p></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h2>\n<div class=\"doc-card-grid cols-2\"><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/concepts/confidence\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 16a8 8 0 1 1 16 0\"></path><path d=\"m12 16 5-6\"></path><path d=\"M7 16h10\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Understand confidence</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/guides/streaming-server\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect height=\"6\" rx=\"1.5\" width=\"16\" x=\"4\" y=\"4\"></rect><rect height=\"6\" rx=\"1.5\" width=\"16\" x=\"4\" y=\"14\"></rect><path d=\"M8 7h.01M8 17h.01M12 7h5M12 17h5\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Stream turns over HTTP</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/guides/python-sdk#stream-turns-explicitly\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8\"></circle><path d=\"M12 7v5l3 2\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Use explicit sessions</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a><a class=\"doc-card linked\" data-pressable=\"true\" href=\"#/backends/light\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"card-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M20 4C12 4 6 9 5 17l-2 3 3-2c8-1 13-7 14-14Z\"></path><path d=\"m6 18 9-9M9 15h4v-4\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"doc-card-copy\"><strong>Choose the light backend</strong></span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"doc-card-arrow\">↗</span></a></div>\n","text":"This quick start uses the api_based backend through the Python SDK. 1. Configure the model endpoint Bash Copy export OPENAI_API_KEY = \"...\" export OPENAI_BASE_URL = \"https://api.openai.com/v1\" export OPENAI_MODEL = \"gpt-class=\" tok-number \">4.1-mini\" 2. Build a graph Python Copy import asyncio from bcg import BCG , BCGMemory , BCGRunner from bcg.llm import LLMClient async def main (): memory = BCGMemory ( graph = BCG ()) runner = BCGRunner ( memory = memory , llm = LLMClient (), backend = \"api_based\" , ) result = await runner . observe_trajectory ( [ { \"role\" : \"user\" , \"content\" : \"Acme is threatening to churn after repeated outages.\" , }, { \"role\" : \"assistant\" , \"content\" : ( \"We should prioritize a reliability review and contact Acme. \" \"This is urgent because the outages are recurring.\" ), }, ], run_id = \"acme-risk-review\" , ) print ( \"beliefs:\" , len ( result . graph . beliefs ())) print ( \"relations:\" , len ( result . graph . relations ())) print ( \"graph:\" , result . output_paths . graph ) print ( \"memory:\" , result . output_paths . memory ) return memory , result memory , result = asyncio . run ( main ()) 3. Inspect beliefs and context Python Copy for belief in memory . graph . beliefs (): print ( belief . id , belief . node_type , belief . confidence , belief . belief , ) print ( memory . context ( task = \"Decide the next customer-success action\" )) 4. Render an HTML graph Bash Copy bcg construct visualize \\ .bcg/runs/acme-risk-review/result.json \\ --output acme-risk-review.html Note observe_trajectory() automatically begins the run, pushes every turn, closes the active session, finalizes the backend, synchronizes the public graph, and writes artifacts. Next steps Understand confidence ↗ Stream turns over HTTP ↗ Use explicit sessions ↗ Choose the light backend ↗","headings":[{"id":"1-configure-the-model-endpoint","text":"1. Configure the model endpoint","level":2},{"id":"2-build-a-graph","text":"2. Build a graph","level":2},{"id":"3-inspect-beliefs-and-context","text":"3. Inspect beliefs and context","level":2},{"id":"4-render-an-html-graph","text":"4. Render an HTML graph","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next steps","level":2}],"icon":"rocket"},"first-graph":{"slug":"first-graph","title":"Your First Graph","description":"Read the result of a BCG construction run.","html":"<p>After a run completes, start with four views of the same state.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-belief-nodes\">1. Belief nodes</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">beliefs</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beliefs</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">beliefs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">({</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"type\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">node_type</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"text\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"stance\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">stance</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"confidence\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">confidence</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"source_role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">role</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"turn\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">turn_index</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">})</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Look for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>propositions that matter to later reasoning</li>\n<li>decision nodes</li>\n<li>stance appropriate to the wording</li>\n<li>source role and turn index</li>\n<li>evidence excerpts that actually support the proposition</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"2-relations\">2. Relations</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">relation</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">relations</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relation</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">from_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relation</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relation</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relation</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">weight</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The direction matters. For <code>depends_on</code>, the source belief depends on the target belief.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-confidence-history\">3. Confidence history</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">belief</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">beliefs</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">initial_confidence</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">evidence_confidence</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">factor_confidence</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">update</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">confidence_history</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">update</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">update</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">update</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reason</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The final score should be explainable through those components and updates.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-provenance\">4. Provenance</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">evidence</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">end</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">match</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">via</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Exact offsets let an inspector highlight the supporting span in the original turn.</p>\n<h2 id=\"use-the-viewer\">Use the viewer</h2>\n<p>The static visualizer is best for one result:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span>outputs/example/result.json</code></pre></div>\n<p>The Live Stream Viewer is best for replaying turn-by-turn graph growth and investigating the final decision. See <a href=\"#/guides/live-stream-viewer\">Live Stream Viewer</a>.</p>\n","text":"After a run completes, start with four views of the same state. 1. Belief nodes python Copy beliefs = result.graph.beliefs() for belief in beliefs: print({ \"id\": belief.id, \"type\": belief.node_type, \"text\": belief.belief, \"stance\": belief.stance, \"confidence\": belief.confidence, \"source_role\": belief.source.role, \"turn\": belief.source.turn_index, }) Look for: propositions that matter to later reasoning decision nodes stance appropriate to the wording source role and turn index evidence excerpts that actually support the proposition 2. Relations python Copy for relation in result.graph.relations(): print( relation.from_id, relation.type, relation.to_id, relation.weight, ) The direction matters. For depends_on , the source belief depends on the target belief. 3. Confidence history python Copy belief = beliefs[0] print(belief.initial_confidence) print(belief.evidence_confidence) print(belief.factor_confidence) for update in belief.confidence_history: print(update.step, update.value, update.reason) The final score should be explainable through those components and updates. 4. Provenance python Copy for excerpt in belief.evidence: print(excerpt.text) print(excerpt.start, excerpt.end, excerpt.match, excerpt.via) print(excerpt.source) Exact offsets let an inspector highlight the supporting span in the original turn. Use the viewer The static visualizer is best for one result: bash Copy bcg construct visualize outputs/example/result.json The Live Stream Viewer is best for replaying turn-by-turn graph growth and investigating the final decision. See Live Stream Viewer .","headings":[{"id":"1-belief-nodes","text":"1. Belief nodes","level":2},{"id":"2-relations","text":"2. Relations","level":2},{"id":"3-confidence-history","text":"3. Confidence history","level":2},{"id":"4-provenance","text":"4. Provenance","level":2},{"id":"use-the-viewer","text":"Use the viewer","level":2}],"icon":"circle-nodes"},"reference-agent":{"slug":"reference-agent","title":"Reference Agent","description":"Use the bundled terminal Agent to experience BCG context management.","html":"<p>The repository includes an interactive terminal Agent as a reference integration. It demonstrates one context policy; it is not a required BCG runtime.</p>\n<h2 id=\"configure\">Configure</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>setup</code></pre></div>\n<p>The setup guide asks for:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Agent authentication and endpoint</li>\n<li>Agent model</li>\n<li>Default context mode: <code>BCG</code> or <code>Default</code></li>\n<li>Managed local graph server or an existing server</li>\n<li><code>api_based</code> or <code>light</code> when BCG manages the server</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Configuration is stored under <code>~/.bcg</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">~/.bcg/config.json\n~/.bcg/.env\n~/.bcg/model_config.json\n~/.bcg/agent/\n~/.bcg/logs/graph-server.log\n~/.bcg/graphs/</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"launch\">Launch</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>bcg agent</code> is an explicit alias.</p>\n<h2 id=\"context-modes\">Context modes</h2>\n<div class=\"offline-tabs\"><div class=\"tab-list\"><button class=\"tab-button active\" data-tab-index=\"0\" type=\"button\">BCG</button><button class=\"tab-button\" data-tab-index=\"1\" type=\"button\">Default</button></div><section class=\"tab-panel active\" data-tab-panel=\"0\"><p>BCG mode:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>permanently retains the initial user input</li>\n<li>keeps the latest two completed turns as raw messages by default</li>\n<li>sends messages leaving that window to graph construction</li>\n<li>injects the current Markdown graph into the system prompt</li>\n<li>disables traditional conversation compaction</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The graph is wrapped in:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-xml\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>XML</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"xml\"><span class=\"nt\">&lt;belief_graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"na\">format=</span><span class=\"s\">\"markdown\"</span><span class=\"nt\">&gt;</span>\n...\n<span class=\"nt\">&lt;/belief_graph&gt;</span></code></pre></div></section><section class=\"tab-panel\" data-tab-panel=\"1\"><p>Default mode keeps the normal Agent conversation and uses automatic compaction. No graph context is injected.</p></section></div>\n<p>The context mode is fixed after the first user message. Start a new session to switch.</p>\n<h2 id=\"terminal-commands\">Terminal commands</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Command</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/help</code></td>\n<td>Commands and keyboard controls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/model</code></td>\n<td>Select the inference model</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/mode</code></td>\n<td>Choose Default or BCG before the first message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/login</code> / <code>/logout</code></td>\n<td>Configure or remove credentials</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/new</code> / <code>/resume</code></td>\n<td>Start or restore a session</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/graph</code></td>\n<td>Check graph connectivity and context policy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/exit</code></td>\n<td>Exit</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"adjust-the-raw-context-window\">Adjust the raw context window</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\"><span class=\"nb\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">BCG_RECENT_TURNS</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;4\nbcg</code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>The reference policy is intentionally opinionated. Custom agents should choose retention and graph-injection rules based on their own latency, safety, and task requirements.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"The repository includes an interactive terminal Agent as a reference integration. It demonstrates one context policy; it is not a required BCG runtime. Configure bash Copy bcg setup The setup guide asks for: Agent authentication and endpoint Agent model Default context mode: BCG or Default Managed local graph server or an existing server api_based or light when BCG manages the server Configuration is stored under ~/.bcg : text Copy ~/.bcg/config.json ~/.bcg/.env ~/.bcg/model_config.json ~/.bcg/agent/ ~/.bcg/logs/graph-server.log ~/.bcg/graphs/ Launch bash Copy bcg bcg agent is an explicit alias. Context modes BCG Default BCG mode: permanently retains the initial user input keeps the latest two completed turns as raw messages by default sends messages leaving that window to graph construction injects the current Markdown graph into the system prompt disables traditional conversation compaction The graph is wrapped in: xml Copy text Copy <belief_graph format=\"markdown\"> ... </belief_graph> Default mode keeps the normal Agent conversation and uses automatic compaction. No graph context is injected. The context mode is fixed after the first user message. Start a new session to switch. Terminal commands Command Purpose /help Commands and keyboard controls /model Select the inference model /mode Choose Default or BCG before the first message /login / /logout Configure or remove credentials /new / /resume Start or restore a session /graph Check graph connectivity and context policy /exit Exit Adjust the raw context window bash Copy export BCG_RECENT_TURNS=4 bcg W Warning The reference policy is intentionally opinionated. Custom agents should choose retention and graph-injection rules based on their own latency, safety, and task requirements.","headings":[{"id":"configure","text":"Configure","level":2},{"id":"launch","text":"Launch","level":2},{"id":"context-modes","text":"Context modes","level":2},{"id":"terminal-commands","text":"Terminal commands","level":2},{"id":"adjust-the-raw-context-window","text":"Adjust the raw context window","level":2}],"icon":"terminal"},"backends/choosing-a-backend":{"slug":"backends/choosing-a-backend","title":"Choosing a Backend","description":"Select `api_based` or `light` based on infrastructure and control requirements.","html":"<p>Both backends produce the same conceptual BCG graph and support batch, replay, HTTP, and <code>BCGRunner</code> workflows.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Choose</th>\n<th>When</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>api_based</code></td>\n<td>You have an OpenAI-compatible model endpoint and want the simplest deployment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>light</code></td>\n<td>You want local embeddings, local stance classification, local NER, and a smaller generative model</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"comparison\">Comparison</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Capability</th>\n<th>api_based</th>\n<th>light</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Default backend</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generative model</td>\n<td>One compatible chat model</td>\n<td>Small model via compatible endpoint</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Embeddings</td>\n<td>Configured local or API embedding provider</td>\n<td>Local sentence-transformers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stance</td>\n<td>API pipeline</td>\n<td>Required local classifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NER</td>\n<td>Extraction pipeline</td>\n<td>Pattern, rules, spaCy ML, or Hugging Face</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Semantic chunking</td>\n<td>Sentence/excerpt modes</td>\n<td>Configurable embedding breakpoint chunks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Configuration</td>\n<td>Stream flags + confidence config</td>\n<td>Full <code>belief_graph</code> config</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Operational complexity</td>\n<td>Lower</td>\n<td>Higher</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Local control</td>\n<td>Moderate</td>\n<td>Higher</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"same-public-commands\">Same public commands</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>data.json\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>light<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>data.json\n\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span>--port<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>light<span class=\"w\"> </span>--port<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848</code></pre></div>\n<p>If the backend positional argument is omitted and the first token is a flag, BCG selects <code>api_based</code> for compatibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recommendation\">Recommendation</h2>\n<p>Start with <code>api_based</code>. Move to <code>light</code> when local model control, local classification, or infrastructure separation matters enough to justify the additional configuration.</p>\n","text":"Both backends produce the same conceptual BCG graph and support batch, replay, HTTP, and BCGRunner workflows. Choose When api_based You have an OpenAI-compatible model endpoint and want the simplest deployment light You want local embeddings, local stance classification, local NER, and a smaller generative model Comparison Capability api_based light Default backend Yes No Generative model One compatible chat model Small model via compatible endpoint Embeddings Configured local or API embedding provider Local sentence-transformers Stance API pipeline Required local classifier NER Extraction pipeline Pattern, rules, spaCy ML, or Hugging Face Semantic chunking Sentence/excerpt modes Configurable embedding breakpoint chunks Configuration Stream flags + confidence config Full belief_graph config Operational complexity Lower Higher Local control Moderate Higher Same public commands Bash Copy bcg construct run api_based --input data.json bcg construct run light --input data.json bcg construct server api_based --port class = \"tok-number\" >8848 bcg construct server light --port class = \"tok-number\" >8848 If the backend positional argument is omitted and the first token is a flag, BCG selects api_based for compatibility. Recommendation Start with api_based . Move to light when local model control, local classification, or infrastructure separation matters enough to justify the additional configuration.","headings":[{"id":"comparison","text":"Comparison","level":2},{"id":"same-public-commands","text":"Same public commands","level":2},{"id":"recommendation","text":"Recommendation","level":2}],"icon":"route"},"backends/api-based":{"slug":"backends/api-based","title":"API-Based Backend","description":"Graph construction with an OpenAI-compatible model and configurable embeddings.","html":"<p><code>api_based</code> is the default construction backend.</p>\n<h2 id=\"start-a-server\">Start a server</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--config<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.bcg/model_config.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--model-key<span class=\"w\"> </span>graph-model<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--embedding-key<span class=\"w\"> </span>embedding<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--host<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;127.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.1<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--port<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output-dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.bcg/graphs</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"batch-construction\">Batch construction</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>trajectory.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--config<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.bcg/model_config.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--model-key<span class=\"w\"> </span>graph-model<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--embedding-key<span class=\"w\"> </span>embedding</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"runtime-options\">Runtime options</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Option</th>\n<th style=\"text-align:right\">Library default</th>\n<th style=\"text-align:right\">Typical CLI default</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>evidence_mode</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>sentence</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>sentence</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>incremental_merge</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>true</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>true</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>incremental_merge_threshold</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>0.8</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>0.86</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>verify_merge</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>false</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">enabled by batch/server layers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>context_chars</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>9000</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>100000</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>min_content_len</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>0</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>0</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<aside class=\"callout info\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M12 10.5v6\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.2\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Info</strong><p>Always confirm the effective command defaults with <code>bcg construct run api_based --help</code> or <code>bcg construct server api_based --help</code>. The public SDK and command layers intentionally have different defaults.</p></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"evidence-choices\">Evidence choices</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\"><span class=\"c1\"># Whole-sentence evidence</span>\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>trajectory.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--evidence-mode<span class=\"w\"> </span>sentence\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># Free-span quoted evidence</span>\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>trajectory.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--evidence-mode<span class=\"w\"> </span>excerpt</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"merge-verification\">Merge verification</h2>\n<p>Verification adds a model call for embedding-flagged candidate groups. The model can reject the merge or rewrite the canonical node to preserve all accepted meaning.</p>\n<p>Use verification when semantic collisions are costly. Disable it when latency and cost matter more than conservative canonicalization.</p>\n","text":"api_based is the default construction backend. Start a server bash Copy bcg construct server api_based \\ --config ~/.bcg/model_config.json \\ --model-key graph-model \\ --embedding-key embedding \\ --host 127.0.0.1 \\ --port 8848 \\ --output-dir ~/.bcg/graphs Batch construction bash Copy bcg construct run api_based \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --config ~/.bcg/model_config.json \\ --model-key graph-model \\ --embedding-key embedding Runtime options Option Library default Typical CLI default evidence_mode sentence sentence incremental_merge true true incremental_merge_threshold 0.8 0.86 verify_merge false enabled by batch/server layers context_chars 9000 100000 min_content_len 0 0 I Info Always confirm the effective command defaults with bcg construct run api_based --help or bcg construct server api_based --help . The public SDK and command layers intentionally have different defaults. Evidence choices bash Copy # Whole-sentence evidence bcg construct run api_based \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --evidence-mode sentence # Free-span quoted evidence bcg construct run api_based \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --evidence-mode excerpt Merge verification Verification adds a model call for embedding-flagged candidate groups. The model can reject the merge or rewrite the canonical node to preserve all accepted meaning. Use verification when semantic collisions are costly. Disable it when latency and cost matter more than conservative canonicalization.","headings":[{"id":"start-a-server","text":"Start a server","level":2},{"id":"batch-construction","text":"Batch construction","level":2},{"id":"runtime-options","text":"Runtime options","level":2},{"id":"evidence-choices","text":"Evidence choices","level":2},{"id":"merge-verification","text":"Merge verification","level":2}],"icon":"server"},"backends/light":{"slug":"backends/light","title":"Light Backend","description":"A locally controlled pipeline with small-model extraction, embeddings, stance, and NER.","html":"<p>The <code>light</code> backend decomposes construction into local or separately served components.</p>\n<h2 id=\"components\">Components</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>small generative extractor through an OpenAI-compatible endpoint</li>\n<li>small generative edge generator</li>\n<li>local sentence-transformers embeddings</li>\n<li>required four-class stance classifier</li>\n<li>local named-entity recognition</li>\n<li>semantic breakpoint chunking</li>\n<li>deterministic confidence and merge pipeline</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"start-supporting-services\">Start supporting services</h2>\n<p>The repository includes helper scripts:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">./scripts/start_vllm.sh\n./scripts/start_sglang_server.sh</code></pre></div>\n<p>For a normal installation, run <code>bcg setup</code>; BCG stores graph model routing in <code>~/.bcg/model_config.json</code>. The repository helper scripts remain available for source development.</p>\n<h2 id=\"run\">Run</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg construct run light \\\n --input trajectory.json \\\n --config ~/.bcg/model_config.json \\\n --model-key gpt-class=\"tok-number\"&gt;5.5 \\\n --embedding-key embedding</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"required-configuration-sections\">Required configuration sections</h2>\n<p>Every key required by the normalizers must be present. Copy the complete template rather than authoring sections from scratch:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">cp<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg/model_config.example.json<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg/model_config.json</code></pre></div>\n<p>The <code>belief_graph</code> block contains:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>extractor</code></li>\n<li><code>stance</code></li>\n<li><code>edge_generation</code></li>\n<li><code>runtime</code></li>\n<li><code>incremental_merge</code></li>\n<li><code>entities</code></li>\n<li><code>confidence</code></li>\n<li><code>chunking</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"when-to-use\">When to use</h2>\n<p>Use <code>light</code> when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>embeddings must remain local</li>\n<li>stance classification needs a dedicated model</li>\n<li>local NER is preferred</li>\n<li>you want independent control over extraction and edge generation</li>\n<li>you can operate the extra model and asset dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>The template contains placeholder local model paths. Replace them before starting the backend.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"The light backend decomposes construction into local or separately served components. Components small generative extractor through an OpenAI-compatible endpoint small generative edge generator local sentence-transformers embeddings required four-class stance classifier local named-entity recognition semantic breakpoint chunking deterministic confidence and merge pipeline Start supporting services The repository includes helper scripts: Bash Copy ./scripts/start_vllm.sh ./scripts/start_sglang_server.sh For a normal installation, run bcg setup ; BCG stores graph model routing in ~/.bcg/model_config.json . The repository helper scripts remain available for source development. Run Bash Copy bcg construct run light \\ --input trajectory.json \\ --config ~/.bcg/model_config.json \\ --model-key gpt-class=\"tok-number\">5.5 \\ --embedding-key embedding Required configuration sections Every key required by the normalizers must be present. Copy the complete template rather than authoring sections from scratch: Bash Copy cp bcg/model_config.example.json bcg/model_config.json The belief_graph block contains: extractor stance edge_generation runtime incremental_merge entities confidence chunking When to use Use light when: embeddings must remain local stance classification needs a dedicated model local NER is preferred you want independent control over extraction and edge generation you can operate the extra model and asset dependencies Warning The template contains placeholder local model paths. Replace them before starting the backend.","headings":[{"id":"components","text":"Components","level":2},{"id":"start-supporting-services","text":"Start supporting services","level":2},{"id":"run","text":"Run","level":2},{"id":"required-configuration-sections","text":"Required configuration sections","level":2},{"id":"when-to-use","text":"When to use","level":2}],"icon":"feather"},"guides/python-sdk":{"slug":"guides/python-sdk","title":"Python SDK","description":"Build, query, and stream BCG graphs inside a Python application.","html":"<p>The public package exports:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code>LLMClient</code> is available separately:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.llm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMConfig</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"construct-a-complete-trajectory\">Construct a complete trajectory</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">asyncio</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.llm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span>\n<span class=\"k\">async</span> <span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">build</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">memory</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n<span class=\"n\">runner</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">llm</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span>\n<span class=\"n\">backend</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"api_based\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">output_root</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\".bcg/runs\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_trajectory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"The payment retry failed twice.\"</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"tool\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"retry_count=class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2; status=declined\"</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"Do not retry automatically; request updated payment details.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"payment-review\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">scenario</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"support\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">item_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"ticket-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;1842\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">counts</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">token_usage</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">asyncio</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"p\">())</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"stream-turns-explicitly\">Stream turns explicitly</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">begin_belief_run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"long-running-investigation\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">backend</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"api_based\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">evidence_mode</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"sentence\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">incremental_merge</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">incremental_merge_threshold</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.84</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start_session</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"day-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2026-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;04\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"Supplier A missed the delivery window.\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tool\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"shipment_status=delayed; eta=class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2026-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"The launch plan depends on the revised supplier ETA.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">end_session</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finalize</span><span class=\"p\">()</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"use-the-resulting-memory\">Use the resulting memory</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">matches</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">believe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"supplier\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">context</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Assess whether launch should be delayed\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">focal_entities</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Supplier A\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_conflicts</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_missing_evidence</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"lifecycle-rules\">Lifecycle rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>one <code>BCGRunner</code> owns one active run at a time</li>\n<li>call <code>begin_belief_run()</code> before manual streaming</li>\n<li><code>observe_turn()</code> creates an implicit session when needed</li>\n<li><code>finalize()</code> may only be called once</li>\n<li>begin a new run after finalization</li>\n<li>snapshots keep <code>memory.graph</code> synchronized</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"custom-model-clients\">Custom model clients</h2>\n<p><code>BCGRunner</code> accepts a client with either:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>async or sync <code>generate(messages, ...)</code></li>\n<li>async or sync <code>generate_text(prompt, ...)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The adapter exposes an OpenAI chat-completions-like shape to construction backends.</p>\n","text":"The public package exports: python Copy from bcg import BCG, BCGMemory, BCGRunner LLMClient is available separately: python Copy from bcg.llm import LLMClient, LLMConfig Construct a complete trajectory python Copy import asyncio from bcg import BCG, BCGMemory, BCGRunner from bcg.llm import LLMClient async def build() -> None: memory = BCGMemory(graph=BCG()) runner = BCGRunner( memory=memory, llm=LLMClient(), backend=\"api_based\", output_root=\".bcg/runs\", ) result = await runner.observe_trajectory( [ {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"The payment retry failed twice.\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"content\": \"retry_count=2; status=declined\"}, { \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Do not retry automatically; request updated payment details.\", }, ], run_id=\"payment-review\", scenario=\"support\", item_id=\"ticket-1842\", ) print(result.counts) print(result.token_usage) asyncio.run(build()) Stream turns explicitly python Copy runner.begin_belief_run( run_id=\"long-running-investigation\", backend=\"api_based\", evidence_mode=\"sentence\", incremental_merge=True, incremental_merge_threshold=0.84, ) runner.start_session(\"day-1\", \"2026-08-04\") await runner.observe_turn(\"user\", \"Supplier A missed the delivery window.\") await runner.observe_turn(\"tool\", \"shipment_status=delayed; eta=2026-08-08\") await runner.observe_turn( \"assistant\", \"The launch plan depends on the revised supplier ETA.\", ) await runner.end_session() result = await runner.finalize() Use the resulting memory python Copy matches = memory.believe(\"supplier\") context = memory.context( task=\"Assess whether launch should be delayed\", focal_entities=[\"Supplier A\"], include_conflicts=True, include_missing_evidence=True, ) Lifecycle rules one BCGRunner owns one active run at a time call begin_belief_run() before manual streaming observe_turn() creates an implicit session when needed finalize() may only be called once begin a new run after finalization snapshots keep memory.graph synchronized Custom model clients BCGRunner accepts a client with either: async or sync generate(messages, ...) async or sync generate_text(prompt, ...) The adapter exposes an OpenAI chat-completions-like shape to construction backends.","headings":[{"id":"construct-a-complete-trajectory","text":"Construct a complete trajectory","level":2},{"id":"stream-turns-explicitly","text":"Stream turns explicitly","level":2},{"id":"use-the-resulting-memory","text":"Use the resulting memory","level":2},{"id":"lifecycle-rules","text":"Lifecycle rules","level":2},{"id":"custom-model-clients","text":"Custom model clients","level":2}],"icon":"python"},"guides/manual-beliefs":{"slug":"guides/manual-beliefs","title":"Manual Beliefs","description":"Insert a known belief without extraction, embeddings, or a model call.","html":"<p>Use <code>BCGMemory.observe()</code> when the input is already the proposition you want to store.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span>\n<span class=\"n\">memory</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n<span class=\"n\">observation</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">source_type</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"manual\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Production deploys require two independent approvals.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">actor</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"policy-bot\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"type\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"service\"</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"n\">observed_at</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2026-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08-04T19:class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;00:00Z\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">metadata</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"policy_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"DEPLOY-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;02\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"environment\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"production\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">observation</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">observation</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">confidence</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"behavior\">Behavior</h2>\n<p>Manual observation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>creates one asserted belief</li>\n<li>uses the complete <code>content</code> string</li>\n<li>records manual evidence</li>\n<li>assigns a source and provenance record</li>\n<li>adds the node to the current in-memory graph</li>\n<li>performs no LLM or embedding call</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"read-it-back\">Read it back</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">believe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"two independent approvals\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Authorize a production deployment\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">focal_entities</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"production\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"p\">))</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"when-not-to-use\">When not to use</h2>\n<p>Do not use manual observation for raw conversations containing multiple propositions. Use <code>BCGRunner</code> so the backend can segment, extract, merge, and link the content.</p>\n","text":"Use BCGMemory.observe() when the input is already the proposition you want to store. python Copy from bcg import BCG, BCGMemory memory = BCGMemory(graph=BCG()) observation = memory.observe( source_type=\"manual\", content=\"Production deploys require two independent approvals.\", actor={\"id\": \"policy-bot\", \"type\": \"service\"}, observed_at=\"2026-08-04T19:00:00Z\", metadata={ \"policy_id\": \"DEPLOY-02\", \"environment\": \"production\", }, ) print(observation.belief.id) print(observation.belief.confidence) Behavior Manual observation: creates one asserted belief uses the complete content string records manual evidence assigns a source and provenance record adds the node to the current in-memory graph performs no LLM or embedding call Read it back python Copy print(memory.believe(\"two independent approvals\")) print(memory.context( task=\"Authorize a production deployment\", focal_entities=[\"production\"], )) When not to use Do not use manual observation for raw conversations containing multiple propositions. Use BCGRunner so the backend can segment, extract, merge, and link the content.","headings":[{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"read-it-back","text":"Read it back","level":2},{"id":"when-not-to-use","text":"When not to use","level":2}],"icon":"brain"},"guides/batch-construction":{"slug":"guides/batch-construction","title":"Batch Construction","description":"Build graphs from trajectory files and benchmark-style datasets.","html":"<p>Use <code>bcg construct run</code> for saved inputs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"basic-command\">Basic command</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg construct run api_based \\\n --input data.json \\\n --config ~/.bcg/model_config.json \\\n --output-dir outputs \\\n --model-key gpt-class=\"tok-number\"&gt;5.5 \\\n --embedding-key embedding</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"common-options\">Common options</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Flag</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--input</code>, <code>-i</code></td>\n<td>required</td>\n<td>JSON or TXT input</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--config</code>, <code>-c</code></td>\n<td><code>bcg/model_config.json</code></td>\n<td>Model configuration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--output-dir</code>, <code>-o</code></td>\n<td><code>outputs</code></td>\n<td>Root directory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--model-key</code></td>\n<td><code>gpt-5.5</code></td>\n<td>Chat model config entry</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--embedding-key</code></td>\n<td><code>embedding</code></td>\n<td>Embedding config entry</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--item</code></td>\n<td>all</td>\n<td>Process one item by ID or index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--keep-order</code></td>\n<td>off</td>\n<td>Preserve multi-session input order</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"select-one-item\">Select one item</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>light<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>dataset.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--item<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;3</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"api-based-controls\">API-based controls</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>data.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--evidence-mode<span class=\"w\"> </span>excerpt<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--incremental-merge-threshold<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.86<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--context-chars<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;100000</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"output-layout\">Output layout</h2>\n<p>Each item receives a subdirectory:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">outputs/&lt;item_id&gt;/\n  result.json\n  final_graph.json\n  token_usage.json\n  events.jsonl\n  logs/\n  ...</code></pre></div>\n<p>See <a href=\"#/reference/output-artifacts\">Output artifacts</a>.</p>\n","text":"Use bcg construct run for saved inputs. Basic command Bash Copy bcg construct run api_based \\ --input data.json \\ --config ~/.bcg/model_config.json \\ --output-dir outputs \\ --model-key gpt-class=\"tok-number\">5.5 \\ --embedding-key embedding Common options Flag Default Purpose --input , -i required JSON or TXT input --config , -c bcg/model_config.json Model configuration --output-dir , -o outputs Root directory --model-key gpt-5.5 Chat model config entry --embedding-key embedding Embedding config entry --item all Process one item by ID or index --keep-order off Preserve multi-session input order Select one item Bash Copy bcg construct run light \\ --input dataset.json \\ --item class = \"tok-number\" >3 API-based controls Bash Copy bcg construct run api_based \\ --input data.json \\ --evidence-mode excerpt \\ --incremental-merge-threshold class = \"tok-number\" >0.86 \\ --context-chars class = \"tok-number\" >100000 Output layout Each item receives a subdirectory: Text Copy outputs/<item_id>/ result.json final_graph.json token_usage.json events.jsonl logs/ ... See Output artifacts .","headings":[{"id":"basic-command","text":"Basic command","level":2},{"id":"common-options","text":"Common options","level":2},{"id":"select-one-item","text":"Select one item","level":2},{"id":"api-based-controls","text":"API-based controls","level":2},{"id":"output-layout","text":"Output layout","level":2}],"icon":"boxes"},"guides/streaming-server":{"slug":"guides/streaming-server","title":"Streaming HTTP Server","description":"Maintain one incremental belief graph per problem ID.","html":"<p>Start the server:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--config<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg/model_config.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--host<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;127.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.1<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--port<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output-dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>outputs_stream</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"push-one-turn\">Push one turn</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-s<span class=\"w\"> </span>-X<span class=\"w\"> </span>POST<span class=\"w\"> </span>http://class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;127.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.1:class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848/turn<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-H<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'content-type: application/json'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-d<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'{</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"problem_id\": \"case-class=\"tok-number\"&gt;42\",</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"role\": \"user\",</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"content\": \"Which alloy resists seawater corrosion best?\"</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">  }'</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Finalize on the last turn:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-s<span class=\"w\"> </span>-X<span class=\"w\"> </span>POST<span class=\"w\"> </span>http://class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;127.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.1:class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848/turn<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-H<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'content-type: application/json'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-d<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'{</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"problem_id\": \"case-class=\"tok-number\"&gt;42\",</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"role\": \"assistant\",</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"content\": \"Titanium grade class=\"tok-number\"&gt;2 is the standard choice.\",</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">    \"is_trajectory_end\": true</span>\n<span class=\"s1\">  }'</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"stream-message-fragments\">Stream message fragments</h2>\n<p>Set <code>is_message_end=false</code> on partial fragments. They are buffered until a final fragment sets <code>is_message_end=true</code> or <code>is_trajectory_end=true</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"case-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;42\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Titanium grade \"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"is_message_end\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"query-the-current-graph\">Query the current graph</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-s<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'http://class=\"tok-number\"&gt;127.0.class=\"tok-number\"&gt;0.1:class=\"tok-number\"&gt;8848/graph?problem_id=case-class=\"tok-number\"&gt;42'</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"release-memory\">Release memory</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-s<span class=\"w\"> </span>-X<span class=\"w\"> </span>POST<span class=\"w\"> </span>http://class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;127.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.1:class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848/release<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-H<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'content-type: application/json'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-d<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'{\"problem_id\":\"case-class=\"tok-number\"&gt;42\"}'</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"concurrency\">Concurrency</h2>\n<p>A separate lock protects each <code>problem_id</code>. Same-problem turns stay ordered; independent problems can run concurrently.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>Do not send the same problem through multiple server processes without sticky routing or external coordination.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"Start the server: bash Copy bcg construct server api_based \\ --config bcg/model_config.json \\ --host 127.0.0.1 \\ --port 8848 \\ --output-dir outputs_stream Push one turn bash Copy curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8848/turn \\ -H 'content-type: application/json' \\ -d '{ \"problem_id\": \"case-42\", \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Which alloy resists seawater corrosion best?\" }' Finalize on the last turn: bash Copy curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8848/turn \\ -H 'content-type: application/json' \\ -d '{ \"problem_id\": \"case-42\", \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Titanium grade 2 is the standard choice.\", \"is_trajectory_end\": true }' Stream message fragments Set is_message_end=false on partial fragments. They are buffered until a final fragment sets is_message_end=true or is_trajectory_end=true . json Copy { \"problem_id\": \"case-42\", \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Titanium grade \", \"is_message_end\": false } Query the current graph bash Copy curl -s \\ 'http://127.0.0.1:8848/graph?problem_id=case-42' Release memory bash Copy curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8848/release \\ -H 'content-type: application/json' \\ -d '{\"problem_id\":\"case-42\"}' Concurrency A separate lock protects each problem_id . Same-problem turns stay ordered; independent problems can run concurrently. W Warning Do not send the same problem through multiple server processes without sticky routing or external coordination.","headings":[{"id":"push-one-turn","text":"Push one turn","level":2},{"id":"stream-message-fragments","text":"Stream message fragments","level":2},{"id":"query-the-current-graph","text":"Query the current graph","level":2},{"id":"release-memory","text":"Release memory","level":2},{"id":"concurrency","text":"Concurrency","level":2}],"icon":"server"},"guides/replay-streams":{"slug":"guides/replay-streams","title":"Replay Streams","description":"Feed an NDJSON turn log through a construction backend.","html":"<p>Replay accepts one turn object per line.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-jsonl\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>jsonl</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"jsonl\"><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"The supplier is late.\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"The release date may need to move.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nt\">\"is_trajectory_end\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"from-a-file\">From a file</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>replay<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--input<span class=\"w\"> </span>turns.jsonl<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--config<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg/model_config.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output-dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>outputs_stream</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"from-standard-input\">From standard input</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">cat<span class=\"w\"> </span>turns.jsonl<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>replay<span class=\"w\"> </span>light</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"end-of-file-finalization\">End-of-file finalization</h2>\n<p>If a trajectory never sends <code>is_trajectory_end</code>, replay finalizes all remaining active problem IDs at end of file.</p>\n<h2 id=\"malformed-lines\">Malformed lines</h2>\n<p>Blank lines are ignored. Malformed JSON and non-object lines produce warnings and are skipped rather than terminating the full replay.</p>\n","text":"Replay accepts one turn object per line. jsonl Copy {\"problem_id\":\"p1\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"The supplier is late.\"} {\"problem_id\":\"p1\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"The release date may need to move.\",\"is_trajectory_end\":true} From a file bash Copy bcg construct replay api_based \\ --input turns.jsonl \\ --config bcg/model_config.json \\ --output-dir outputs_stream From standard input bash Copy cat turns.jsonl | bcg construct replay light End-of-file finalization If a trajectory never sends is_trajectory_end , replay finalizes all remaining active problem IDs at end of file. Malformed lines Blank lines are ignored. Malformed JSON and non-object lines produce warnings and are skipped rather than terminating the full replay.","headings":[{"id":"from-a-file","text":"From a file","level":2},{"id":"from-standard-input","text":"From standard input","level":2},{"id":"end-of-file-finalization","text":"End-of-file finalization","level":2},{"id":"malformed-lines","text":"Malformed lines","level":2}],"icon":"clock-rotate-left"},"guides/custom-agent-integration":{"slug":"guides/custom-agent-integration","title":"Custom Agent Integration","description":"Add BCG to an existing agent without adopting the reference Agent.","html":"<p>BCG is agent-independent. Your integration needs three decisions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>how turns reach graph construction</li>\n<li>how graph state is rendered for the model</li>\n<li>when confidence or conflicts block action</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"integration-patterns\">Integration patterns</h2>\n<div class=\"offline-tabs\"><div class=\"tab-list\"><button class=\"tab-button active\" data-tab-index=\"0\" type=\"button\">Python in-process</button><button class=\"tab-button\" data-tab-index=\"1\" type=\"button\">HTTP service</button><button class=\"tab-button\" data-tab-index=\"2\" type=\"button\">Offline reconstruction</button></div><section class=\"tab-panel active\" data-tab-panel=\"0\"><p>Use <code>BCGRunner</code> and keep <code>BCGMemory</code> beside your agent state.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">snapshot</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">role</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">context</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">current_task</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div></section><section class=\"tab-panel\" data-tab-panel=\"1\"><p>Push turns from any language:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-http\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>HTTP</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"http\"><span class=\"err\">POST /turn</span>\n<span class=\"err\">Content-Type: application/json</span>\n<span class=\"err\">{</span>\n<span class=\"err\">  \"problem_id\": \"agent-session-id\",</span>\n<span class=\"err\">  \"role\": \"tool\",</span>\n<span class=\"err\">  \"content\": \"inventory=class=\"tok-number\"&gt;0\"</span>\n<span class=\"err\">}</span></code></pre></div></section><section class=\"tab-panel\" data-tab-panel=\"2\"><p>Save the trajectory, then run <code>bcg construct run</code> after completion for audit and evaluation.</p></section></div>\n<h2 id=\"recommended-message-mapping\">Recommended message mapping</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Agent event</th>\n<th>BCG role</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>User input</td>\n<td><code>user</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assistant reasoning or output</td>\n<td><code>assistant</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tool result</td>\n<td><code>tool</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Function result</td>\n<td><code>function</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>System policy</td>\n<td><code>system</code> when intentionally included</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"context-injection\">Context injection</h2>\n<p>A minimal policy:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">graph_context</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">current_task</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">focal_entities</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">current_entities</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_conflicts</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_missing_evidence</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">system_prompt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">base_system_prompt</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"se\">\\n\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"n\">graph_context</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Production policies should filter by authorization, source role, confidence, recency, and task relevance.</p>\n<h2 id=\"action-gating\">Action gating</h2>\n<p>BCG does not execute actions. Your agent can use graph state to require:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>minimum confidence</li>\n<li>no unresolved contradiction</li>\n<li>supporting evidence present</li>\n<li>specific source classes</li>\n<li>human confirmation for decision nodes</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"session-cleanup\">Session cleanup</h2>\n<p>Finalize the graph when a task ends. When using the HTTP server, call <code>/release</code> after artifacts have been consumed and the in-memory session is no longer needed.</p>\n","text":"BCG is agent-independent. Your integration needs three decisions: how turns reach graph construction how graph state is rendered for the model when confidence or conflicts block action Integration patterns Python in-process HTTP service Offline reconstruction Use BCGRunner and keep BCGMemory beside your agent state. python Copy text Copy snapshot = await runner.observe_turn(role, content) context = memory.context(task=current_task) Push turns from any language: http Copy text Copy POST /turn Content-Type: application/json { \"problem_id\": \"agent-session-id\", \"role\": \"tool\", \"content\": \"inventory=0\" } Save the trajectory, then run bcg construct run after completion for audit and evaluation. Recommended message mapping Agent event BCG role User input user Assistant reasoning or output assistant Tool result tool Function result function System policy system when intentionally included Context injection A minimal policy: python Copy graph_context = memory.context( task=current_task, focal_entities=current_entities, include_conflicts=True, include_missing_evidence=True, ) system_prompt = base_system_prompt + \"\\n\\n\" + graph_context Production policies should filter by authorization, source role, confidence, recency, and task relevance. Action gating BCG does not execute actions. Your agent can use graph state to require: minimum confidence no unresolved contradiction supporting evidence present specific source classes human confirmation for decision nodes Session cleanup Finalize the graph when a task ends. When using the HTTP server, call /release after artifacts have been consumed and the in-memory session is no longer needed.","headings":[{"id":"integration-patterns","text":"Integration patterns","level":2},{"id":"recommended-message-mapping","text":"Recommended message mapping","level":2},{"id":"context-injection","text":"Context injection","level":2},{"id":"action-gating","text":"Action gating","level":2},{"id":"session-cleanup","text":"Session cleanup","level":2}],"icon":"plug"},"guides/live-stream-viewer":{"slug":"guides/live-stream-viewer","title":"Live Stream Viewer","description":"Replay trajectory growth, inspect graph evidence, and audit final decisions.","html":"<p>The live viewer is located at:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">dashboard/bcg_viewer/belief_graph_stream_viewer.html</code></pre></div>\n<p>Its visual language also defines this documentation theme: warm paper background, white panels, brick-red primary actions, teal selection, yellow evidence, and role-specific node colors.</p>\n<h2 id=\"start-the-viewer-backend\">Start the viewer backend</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\"><span class=\"nb\">cd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>dashboard/bcg_viewer\npython3<span class=\"w\"> </span>serve_viewer.py</code></pre></div>\n<p>Open:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">http://class=\"tok-number\"&gt;127.0.class=\"tok-number\"&gt;0.1:class=\"tok-number\"&gt;8123/belief_graph_stream_viewer.html</code></pre></div>\n<p>The server discovers stream outputs and enables <strong>Run new case</strong> when the configured benchmark and construction commands are available.</p>\n<h2 id=\"replay-only-mode\">Replay-only mode</h2>\n<p>Open the HTML file and choose a folder containing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>complete stream sample directories</li>\n<li>standalone compatible <code>result.json</code> files</li>\n<li>or both</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The viewer discovers compatible files recursively and avoids duplicate entries.</p>\n<h2 id=\"main-panels\">Main panels</h2>\n<h3 id=\"conversation-trajectory\">Conversation trajectory</h3>\n<p>The left panel streams messages and highlights evidence spans linked to beliefs.</p>\n<h3 id=\"graph-canvas\">Graph canvas</h3>\n<p>The graph rebuilds after each turn. New nodes flash. Relation styles distinguish:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>depends_on</code></li>\n<li><code>supplements</code></li>\n<li><code>contradicts</code></li>\n<li>legacy/supportive relations when present</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"inspector\">Inspector</h3>\n<p>Click a node or edge to inspect text, source, confidence, entities, evidence, and relation details.</p>\n<h3 id=\"run-insights\">Run insights</h3>\n<p>The viewer can summarize graph growth, timing phases, merge behavior, confidence history, and the final decision path when those fields are present.</p>\n<h2 id=\"selection-workflow\">Selection workflow</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>click normally to inspect</li>\n<li>Ctrl-click on Windows/Linux or Command-click on macOS to select nodes</li>\n<li>choose <strong>View subgraph</strong></li>\n<li>optionally include direct neighbors</li>\n<li>press Escape to clear inspection</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"timing-badges\">Timing badges</h2>\n<p>When artifacts include timing data, the trajectory can show:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>agent generation</li>\n<li>tool execution</li>\n<li>node generation</li>\n<li>merge</li>\n<li>LLM merge check</li>\n<li>edge generation</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"supported-data\">Supported data</h2>\n<p>The viewer normalizes multiple schema generations, including <code>all_nodes</code> or <code>nodes</code>, legacy relation names, <code>trajectory_index</code> or <code>turn_id</code>, and graph-level evidence records.</p>\n","text":"The live viewer is located at: text Copy dashboard/bcg_viewer/belief_graph_stream_viewer.html Its visual language also defines this documentation theme: warm paper background, white panels, brick-red primary actions, teal selection, yellow evidence, and role-specific node colors. Start the viewer backend bash Copy cd dashboard/bcg_viewer python3 serve_viewer.py Open: text Copy http://127.0.0.1:8123/belief_graph_stream_viewer.html The server discovers stream outputs and enables Run new case when the configured benchmark and construction commands are available. Replay-only mode Open the HTML file and choose a folder containing: complete stream sample directories standalone compatible result.json files or both The viewer discovers compatible files recursively and avoids duplicate entries. Main panels Conversation trajectory The left panel streams messages and highlights evidence spans linked to beliefs. Graph canvas The graph rebuilds after each turn. New nodes flash. Relation styles distinguish: depends_on supplements contradicts legacy/supportive relations when present Inspector Click a node or edge to inspect text, source, confidence, entities, evidence, and relation details. Run insights The viewer can summarize graph growth, timing phases, merge behavior, confidence history, and the final decision path when those fields are present. Selection workflow click normally to inspect Ctrl-click on Windows/Linux or Command-click on macOS to select nodes choose View subgraph optionally include direct neighbors press Escape to clear inspection Timing badges When artifacts include timing data, the trajectory can show: agent generation tool execution node generation merge LLM merge check edge generation Supported data The viewer normalizes multiple schema generations, including all_nodes or nodes , legacy relation names, trajectory_index or turn_id , and graph-level evidence records.","headings":[{"id":"start-the-viewer-backend","text":"Start the viewer backend","level":2},{"id":"replay-only-mode","text":"Replay-only mode","level":2},{"id":"main-panels","text":"Main panels","level":2},{"id":"conversation-trajectory","text":"Conversation trajectory","level":3},{"id":"graph-canvas","text":"Graph canvas","level":3},{"id":"inspector","text":"Inspector","level":3},{"id":"run-insights","text":"Run insights","level":3},{"id":"selection-workflow","text":"Selection workflow","level":2},{"id":"timing-badges","text":"Timing badges","level":2},{"id":"supported-data","text":"Supported data","level":2}],"icon":"eye"},"guides/static-visualization":{"slug":"guides/static-visualization","title":"Static Visualization","description":"Generate a self-contained HTML inspector for one graph result.","html":"<p>Use the built-in renderer:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span>outputs/case-class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;42/result.json</code></pre></div>\n<p>Supported inputs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>result.json</code></li>\n<li><code>final_graph.json</code></li>\n<li><code>belief_graph.jsonl</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Choose an output path:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>outputs/case-class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;42/final_graph.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output<span class=\"w\"> </span>reports/case-class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;42.html</code></pre></div>\n<p>The generated file is self-contained and includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>conversation trajectory</li>\n<li>evidence highlighting</li>\n<li>graph layout by source turn</li>\n<li>role and node-type colors</li>\n<li>relation paths</li>\n<li>node, edge, factor, confidence, timing, and audit inspection</li>\n<li>summary counts</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"static-vs-live-viewer\">Static vs live viewer</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Use static visualization when</th>\n<th>Use live viewer when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Sharing one finalized result</td>\n<td>Replaying graph growth</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No server should be required</td>\n<td>Comparing samples</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Embedding an artifact in a report</td>\n<td>Running a new case</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Inspecting final state</td>\n<td>Investigating timing and per-turn changes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","text":"Use the built-in renderer: bash Copy bcg construct visualize outputs/case-42/result.json Supported inputs: result.json final_graph.json belief_graph.jsonl Choose an output path: bash Copy bcg construct visualize \\ outputs/case-42/final_graph.json \\ --output reports/case-42.html The generated file is self-contained and includes: conversation trajectory evidence highlighting graph layout by source turn role and node-type colors relation paths node, edge, factor, confidence, timing, and audit inspection summary counts Static vs live viewer Use static visualization when Use live viewer when Sharing one finalized result Replaying graph growth No server should be required Comparing samples Embedding an artifact in a report Running a new case Inspecting final state Investigating timing and per-turn changes","headings":[{"id":"static-vs-live-viewer","text":"Static vs live viewer","level":2}],"icon":"chart-network"},"guides/audit-a-decision":{"slug":"guides/audit-a-decision","title":"Audit a Decision","description":"Trace a final decision from output text back through beliefs, evidence, and confidence.","html":"<p>A decision audit should answer four questions.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-what-was-decided\">1. What was decided?</h2>\n<p>Find nodes with:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">decisions</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"n\">belief</span>\n<span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beliefs</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">node_type</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"decision\"</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Confirm the canonical decision text and source turn.</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-what-did-it-depend-on\">2. What did it depend on?</h2>\n<p>Traverse incoming or outgoing <code>depends_on</code> relations according to the decision's graph position.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">relations</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">relation_dicts</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"depends_on\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Inspect each relation note, weight, and activation condition.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-which-evidence-supports-each-belief\">3. Which evidence supports each belief?</h2>\n<p>For every node in the decision path:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">belief</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">evidence</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">excerpt</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">end</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Compare the highlighted excerpt against the original trajectory turn.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-how-did-confidence-change\">4. How did confidence change?</h2>\n<p>Review:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>initial_confidence</code></li>\n<li><code>evidence_confidence</code></li>\n<li><code>factor_confidence</code></li>\n<li>every <code>confidence_history</code> entry</li>\n<li>contradictions and their activation state</li>\n<li>merges that changed the canonical node</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"viewer-workflow\">Viewer workflow</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>replay the sample to the final turn</li>\n<li>click <strong>Explain final decision</strong></li>\n<li>inspect the decision path</li>\n<li>open each node's evidence</li>\n<li>review confidence history</li>\n<li>inspect merge records for rewritten nodes</li>\n<li>export or retain <code>result.json</code>, prompt logs, and timing artifacts</li>\n</ol>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>A clear graph path is evidence of system traceability, not proof that the decision is correct. Human or domain-specific validation remains necessary.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"A decision audit should answer four questions. 1. What was decided? Find nodes with: python Copy decisions = [ belief for belief in result.graph.beliefs() if belief.node_type == \"decision\" ] Confirm the canonical decision text and source turn. 2. What did it depend on? Traverse incoming or outgoing depends_on relations according to the decision's graph position. python Copy relations = result.graph.relation_dicts(\"depends_on\") Inspect each relation note, weight, and activation condition. 3. Which evidence supports each belief? For every node in the decision path: python Copy for excerpt in belief.evidence: print(excerpt.text, excerpt.start, excerpt.end) Compare the highlighted excerpt against the original trajectory turn. 4. How did confidence change? Review: initial_confidence evidence_confidence factor_confidence every confidence_history entry contradictions and their activation state merges that changed the canonical node Viewer workflow replay the sample to the final turn click Explain final decision inspect the decision path open each node's evidence review confidence history inspect merge records for rewritten nodes export or retain result.json , prompt logs, and timing artifacts W Warning A clear graph path is evidence of system traceability, not proof that the decision is correct. Human or domain-specific validation remains necessary.","headings":[{"id":"1-what-was-decided","text":"1. What was decided?","level":2},{"id":"2-what-did-it-depend-on","text":"2. What did it depend on?","level":2},{"id":"3-which-evidence-supports-each-belief","text":"3. Which evidence supports each belief?","level":2},{"id":"4-how-did-confidence-change","text":"4. How did confidence change?","level":2},{"id":"viewer-workflow","text":"Viewer workflow","level":2}],"icon":"magnifying-glass-chart"},"guides/benchmarking":{"slug":"guides/benchmarking","title":"Benchmarking","description":"Compare the reference Agent in Default and BCG context modes.","html":"<p>The benchmark adapter runs supported datasets through the bundled Agent and writes trajectories plus summary metrics.</p>\n<h2 id=\"basic-command\">Basic command</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>benchmark<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>hotpotqa<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--data-root<span class=\"w\"> </span>datasets<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--modes<span class=\"w\"> </span>default,bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--model<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$OPENAI_MODEL</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--base-url<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"nv\">$OPENAI_BASE_URL</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"supported-benchmark-names\">Supported benchmark names</h2>\n<p>The exact list is exposed by the CLI:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>benchmark<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help</code></pre></div>\n<p>The repository includes adapters for the benchmark set declared in <code>bcg.benchmark.loaders.BENCHMARKS</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"important-controls\">Important controls</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Option</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--modes</code></td>\n<td>Comma-separated <code>default,bcg</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--max-problems</code></td>\n<td>Limit examples; <code>0</code> means all</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--task-ids</code></td>\n<td>Select exact IDs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--shuffle/--no-shuffle</code></td>\n<td>Shuffle before truncation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--workers</code></td>\n<td>Concurrent Agent processes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--timeout</code></td>\n<td>Per-task timeout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--graph-url</code></td>\n<td>Graph server for BCG mode</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--graph-max-turns</code></td>\n<td>Maximum graph messages</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--recent-turns</code></td>\n<td>Raw completed turns retained</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--allow-graph-fallback</code></td>\n<td>Score tasks that fell back to raw context</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>--overwrite</code></td>\n<td>Rerun existing task artifacts</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"fair-comparison\">Fair comparison</h2>\n<p>Keep constant:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>agent model and endpoint</li>\n<li>tool availability</li>\n<li>benchmark sample selection</li>\n<li>timeout</li>\n<li>judge model where applicable</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Change only context mode and the BCG policy parameters being evaluated.</p>\n<h2 id=\"interpret-results-carefully\">Interpret results carefully</h2>\n<p>Measure more than final accuracy:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>cumulative token cost over task horizon</li>\n<li>latency by turn</li>\n<li>graph construction cost</li>\n<li>graph fallback rate</li>\n<li>contradiction and merge behavior</li>\n<li>decision trace quality</li>\n<li>evidence grounding</li>\n</ul>\n","text":"The benchmark adapter runs supported datasets through the bundled Agent and writes trajectories plus summary metrics. Basic command bash Copy bcg benchmark run hotpotqa \\ --data-root datasets \\ --modes default,bcg \\ --model \"$OPENAI_MODEL\" \\ --base-url \"$OPENAI_BASE_URL\" Supported benchmark names The exact list is exposed by the CLI: bash Copy bcg benchmark run --help The repository includes adapters for the benchmark set declared in bcg.benchmark.loaders.BENCHMARKS . Important controls Option Purpose --modes Comma-separated default,bcg --max-problems Limit examples; 0 means all --task-ids Select exact IDs --shuffle/--no-shuffle Shuffle before truncation --workers Concurrent Agent processes --timeout Per-task timeout --graph-url Graph server for BCG mode --graph-max-turns Maximum graph messages --recent-turns Raw completed turns retained --allow-graph-fallback Score tasks that fell back to raw context --overwrite Rerun existing task artifacts Fair comparison Keep constant: agent model and endpoint tool availability benchmark sample selection timeout judge model where applicable Change only context mode and the BCG policy parameters being evaluated. Interpret results carefully Measure more than final accuracy: cumulative token cost over task horizon latency by turn graph construction cost graph fallback rate contradiction and merge behavior decision trace quality evidence grounding","headings":[{"id":"basic-command","text":"Basic command","level":2},{"id":"supported-benchmark-names","text":"Supported benchmark names","level":2},{"id":"important-controls","text":"Important controls","level":2},{"id":"fair-comparison","text":"Fair comparison","level":2},{"id":"interpret-results-carefully","text":"Interpret results carefully","level":2}],"icon":"gauge"},"guides/tracing":{"slug":"guides/tracing","title":"Tracing","description":"Enable optional Langfuse spans around BCG execution.","html":"<p>BCG tracing is optional and designed to be best-effort.</p>\n<h2 id=\"enable\">Enable</h2>\n<p>Configure Langfuse through its standard environment variables, then enable BCG tracing in the runtime environment expected by <code>bcg.tracing</code>.</p>\n<p>When tracing is not configured, the decorators and update helpers become no-ops.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-module-provides\">What the module provides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>trace()</code> decorator</li>\n<li><code>update_current_span()</code></li>\n<li><code>update_current_generation()</code></li>\n<li><code>flush_traces()</code></li>\n<li><code>is_tracing_enabled()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"local-artifacts-remain-authoritative\">Local artifacts remain authoritative</h2>\n<p>Even with remote tracing enabled, retain BCG's run artifacts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>prompts</li>\n<li>embedding calls</li>\n<li>merge logs</li>\n<li>events</li>\n<li>token usage</li>\n<li>timing</li>\n<li>final graph</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These files provide graph-specific detail that a generic trace backend may not capture.</p>\n","text":"BCG tracing is optional and designed to be best-effort. Enable Configure Langfuse through its standard environment variables, then enable BCG tracing in the runtime environment expected by bcg.tracing . When tracing is not configured, the decorators and update helpers become no-ops. What the module provides trace() decorator update_current_span() update_current_generation() flush_traces() is_tracing_enabled() Local artifacts remain authoritative Even with remote tracing enabled, retain BCG's run artifacts: prompts embedding calls merge logs events token usage timing final graph These files provide graph-specific detail that a generic trace backend may not capture.","headings":[{"id":"enable","text":"Enable","level":2},{"id":"what-the-module-provides","text":"What the module provides","level":2},{"id":"local-artifacts-remain-authoritative","text":"Local artifacts remain authoritative","level":2}],"icon":"activity"},"reference/bcg":{"slug":"reference/bcg","title":"BCG","description":"Reference for the in-memory graph container.","html":"<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCG</span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code>BCG</code> is a Pydantic model containing:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">edges</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">merges</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">sessions</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">evidence</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">factors</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">metadata</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">{},</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"node-operations\">Node operations</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add_node(node)</code></td>\n<td>Async generic node insertion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add_belief(belief)</code></td>\n<td>Create and append a belief node</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>next_belief_id()</code></td>\n<td>Read the next monotonic ID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>allocate_belief_id()</code></td>\n<td>Reserve a stable ID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>node_for_belief_id(id)</code></td>\n<td>Find a node</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>update_belief(payload)</code></td>\n<td>Replace payload while preserving UUID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>remove_belief(id)</code></td>\n<td>Remove node and optionally incident edges</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>belief_nodes()</code></td>\n<td>Ordered belief nodes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>beliefs()</code></td>\n<td>Ordered typed payloads</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>belief_dicts()</code></td>\n<td>JSON-compatible active beliefs</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"relation-operations\">Relation operations</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add_edge(edge)</code></td>\n<td>Async generic edge insertion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add_relation(payload, source_uuid, target_uuid)</code></td>\n<td>Create a typed edge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add_relation_by_ids(payload)</code></td>\n<td>Resolve endpoints by belief ID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>add_relations(dicts)</code></td>\n<td>Validate and add relation dictionaries</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>relations(type=None)</code></td>\n<td>Return typed relations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>relation_dicts(type=None)</code></td>\n<td>Return JSON-compatible relations</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>remap_relations(mapping)</code></td>\n<td>Rewire endpoints after merges</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"serialization\">Serialization</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">json_text</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">model_dump_json</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">indent</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">memory_shape</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to_memory_dict</span><span class=\"p\">()</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"mutation-note\">Mutation note</h2>\n<p>The public graph is an in-memory container. Persist it explicitly or use <code>BCGRunner</code>, which writes run artifacts during finalization.</p>\n","text":"python Copy from bcg import BCG BCG is a Pydantic model containing: python Copy BCG( nodes=[], edges=[], merges=[], sessions=[], evidence=[], factors=[], metadata={}, ) Node operations Method Purpose add_node(node) Async generic node insertion add_belief(belief) Create and append a belief node next_belief_id() Read the next monotonic ID allocate_belief_id() Reserve a stable ID node_for_belief_id(id) Find a node update_belief(payload) Replace payload while preserving UUID remove_belief(id) Remove node and optionally incident edges belief_nodes() Ordered belief nodes beliefs() Ordered typed payloads belief_dicts() JSON-compatible active beliefs Relation operations Method Purpose add_edge(edge) Async generic edge insertion add_relation(payload, source_uuid, target_uuid) Create a typed edge add_relation_by_ids(payload) Resolve endpoints by belief ID add_relations(dicts) Validate and add relation dictionaries relations(type=None) Return typed relations relation_dicts(type=None) Return JSON-compatible relations remap_relations(mapping) Rewire endpoints after merges Serialization python Copy json_text = graph.model_dump_json(indent=2) memory_shape = graph.to_memory_dict() Mutation note The public graph is an in-memory container. Persist it explicitly or use BCGRunner , which writes run artifacts during finalization.","headings":[{"id":"node-operations","text":"Node operations","level":2},{"id":"relation-operations","text":"Relation operations","level":2},{"id":"serialization","text":"Serialization","level":2},{"id":"mutation-note","text":"Mutation note","level":2}],"icon":"circle-nodes"},"reference/memory":{"slug":"reference/memory","title":"BCGMemory","description":"Reference for the application-facing memory facade.","html":"<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"constructor\">Constructor</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">namespace</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"default\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">options</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">{},</span>\n<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">confidence_config</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>A graph is created lazily when needed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"observe\"><code>observe()</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">observation</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">source_type</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"manual\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"A known proposition.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">actor</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">observed_at</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">metadata</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Returns <code>MemoryObservation</code> with:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>belief</code></li>\n<li><code>graph</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The method performs no LLM extraction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"believe\"><code>believe()</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">matches</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">believe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"substring\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Returns belief dictionaries whose text matches the target substring.</p>\n<h2 id=\"context\"><code>context()</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">text</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">task</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Plan the next action\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">focal_entities</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Acme\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">max_variables</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_conflicts</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_missing_evidence</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Assembles a Markdown-like task context from the current graph.</p>\n<h2 id=\"search\"><code>search()</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">results</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">search</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">query</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"outage risk\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">max_results</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_conflicts</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">include_missing_evidence</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The current implementation searches belief text in the in-memory graph. It is not a vector database API.</p>\n","text":"python Copy from bcg import BCGMemory Constructor python Copy BCGMemory( namespace=\"default\", options={}, graph=None, confidence_config=None, ) A graph is created lazily when needed. observe() python Copy observation = memory.observe( source_type=\"manual\", content=\"A known proposition.\", actor=None, observed_at=None, metadata=None, ) Returns MemoryObservation with: belief graph The method performs no LLM extraction. believe() python Copy matches = memory.believe(\"substring\") Returns belief dictionaries whose text matches the target substring. context() python Copy text = memory.context( task=\"Plan the next action\", focal_entities=[\"Acme\"], max_variables=100, include_conflicts=True, include_missing_evidence=True, ) Assembles a Markdown-like task context from the current graph. search() python Copy results = await memory.search( query=\"outage risk\", max_results=10, include_conflicts=True, include_missing_evidence=True, ) The current implementation searches belief text in the in-memory graph. It is not a vector database API.","headings":[{"id":"constructor","text":"Constructor","level":2},{"id":"observe","text":"observe()","level":2},{"id":"believe","text":"believe()","level":2},{"id":"context","text":"context()","level":2},{"id":"search","text":"search()","level":2}],"icon":"brain"},"reference/runner":{"slug":"reference/runner","title":"BCGRunner","description":"Reference for graph-construction lifecycle orchestration.","html":"<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"constructor\">Constructor</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">llm</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">llm</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">output_root</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\".bcg/runs\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">backend</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"api_based\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"complete-trajectory\">Complete trajectory</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_trajectory</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">trajectory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">model</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">max_tokens</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">scenario</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"research\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">item_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"trajectory\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">backend</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">evidence_mode</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"sentence\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">incremental_merge</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">incremental_merge_threshold</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">verify_merge</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">False</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">context_chars</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">9000</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">io_context_chars</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">6000</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">min_content_len</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">belief_graph_config</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">embedder</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">metadata</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">options</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"explicit-lifecycle\">Explicit lifecycle</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">begin_belief_run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start_session</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">session_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">date</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">snapshot</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe_turn</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">role</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">content</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">date</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">has_answer</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">summary</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">end_session</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">result</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">runner</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finalize</span><span class=\"p\">()</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"result\">Result</h2>\n<p><code>BeliefGraphRunResult</code> contains:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Field</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>run_id</code></td>\n<td>Stable run identifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>graph</code></td>\n<td>Final public <code>BCG</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>memory</code></td>\n<td>Serialized memory document</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output_paths</code></td>\n<td>Typed artifact paths</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>token_usage</code></td>\n<td>Construction usage totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>counts</code></td>\n<td>Node, relation, and related counts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>construct_result</code></td>\n<td>Native backend result</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"errors\">Errors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>calling turn operations without an active run raises <code>RuntimeError</code></li>\n<li>beginning a second active run is invalid</li>\n<li>starting a session while one is active is invalid</li>\n<li>calling <code>finalize()</code> twice is invalid</li>\n</ul>\n","text":"python Copy from bcg import BCGRunner Constructor python Copy BCGRunner( memory=memory, llm=llm, output_root=\".bcg/runs\", backend=\"api_based\", ) Complete trajectory python Copy result = await runner.observe_trajectory( trajectory, run_id=None, model=None, max_tokens=None, scenario=\"research\", item_id=\"trajectory\", backend=None, evidence_mode=\"sentence\", incremental_merge=True, incremental_merge_threshold=0.8, verify_merge=False, context_chars=9000, io_context_chars=6000, min_content_len=0, belief_graph_config=None, embedder=None, metadata=None, options=None, ) Explicit lifecycle python Copy runner.begin_belief_run(...) runner.start_session(session_id, date=None) snapshot = await runner.observe_turn(role, content, date=None, has_answer=None) summary = await runner.end_session() result = await runner.finalize() Result BeliefGraphRunResult contains: Field Meaning run_id Stable run identifier graph Final public BCG memory Serialized memory document output_paths Typed artifact paths token_usage Construction usage totals counts Node, relation, and related counts construct_result Native backend result Errors calling turn operations without an active run raises RuntimeError beginning a second active run is invalid starting a session while one is active is invalid calling finalize() twice is invalid","headings":[{"id":"constructor","text":"Constructor","level":2},{"id":"complete-trajectory","text":"Complete trajectory","level":2},{"id":"explicit-lifecycle","text":"Explicit lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"result","text":"Result","level":2},{"id":"errors","text":"Errors","level":2}],"icon":"play"},"reference/llm-client":{"slug":"reference/llm-client","title":"LLM Client","description":"OpenAI-compatible model and embedding clients used by the public SDK.","html":"<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.llm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">EmbeddingClient</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">EmbeddingConfig</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">LLMConfig</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">TokenUsageTracker</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"llmclient\"><code>LLMClient</code></h2>\n<p>Async methods:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>generate(messages, ...)</code></li>\n<li><code>generate_text(prompt, ...)</code></li>\n<li><code>generate_json(prompt, ...)</code></li>\n<li><code>image(image_bytes, ...)</code></li>\n<li><code>close()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The client uses the OpenAI Responses API shape, retries retryable failures, supports tool dispatch, and records usage.</p>\n<h2 id=\"example\">Example</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg.llm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMConfig</span>\n<span class=\"n\">client</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">LLMClient</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">LLMConfig</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"n\">api_key</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"...\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">base_url</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://api.openai.com/v1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">model</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"gpt-class=\"</span><span class=\"n\">tok</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">number</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;4.1-mini\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">text</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">client</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">generate_text</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">\"Return one sentence describing the incident.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">label</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"incident_summary\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"embeddingclient\"><code>EmbeddingClient</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"n\">vectors</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">embedder</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">embed</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"first belief\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"second belief\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"n\">purpose</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"incremental_merge\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code>EmbeddingConfig</code> makes provider, model, dimensions, batch size, and local settings explicit.</p>\n<h2 id=\"token-usage\">Token usage</h2>\n<p><code>TokenUsageTracker</code> aggregates records by label and total. BCG writes usage artifacts when the backend returns token counts; otherwise it may estimate counts from text.</p>\n","text":"python Copy from bcg.llm import ( EmbeddingClient, EmbeddingConfig, LLMClient, LLMConfig, TokenUsageTracker, ) LLMClient Async methods: generate(messages, ...) generate_text(prompt, ...) generate_json(prompt, ...) image(image_bytes, ...) close() The client uses the OpenAI Responses API shape, retries retryable failures, supports tool dispatch, and records usage. Example python Copy from bcg.llm import LLMClient, LLMConfig client = LLMClient( LLMConfig( api_key=\"...\", base_url=\"https://api.openai.com/v1\", model=\"gpt-4.1-mini\", ) ) text = await client.generate_text( \"Return one sentence describing the incident.\", label=\"incident_summary\", ) EmbeddingClient python Copy vectors = embedder.embed( [\"first belief\", \"second belief\"], purpose=\"incremental_merge\", ) EmbeddingConfig makes provider, model, dimensions, batch size, and local settings explicit. Token usage TokenUsageTracker aggregates records by label and total. BCG writes usage artifacts when the backend returns token counts; otherwise it may estimate counts from text.","headings":[{"id":"llmclient","text":"LLMClient","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"embeddingclient","text":"EmbeddingClient","level":2},{"id":"token-usage","text":"Token usage","level":2}],"icon":"bot"},"reference/cli":{"slug":"reference/cli","title":"CLI Reference","description":"Top-level BCG commands and construction workflows.","html":"<h2 id=\"top-level\">Top-level</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>agent\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>setup\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>benchmark\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>--version</code></pre></div>\n<p>Running <code>bcg</code> without a subcommand opens the reference Agent.</p>\n<h2 id=\"construction\">Construction</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>&lt;backend&gt;<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>options<span class=\"o\">]</span>\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>&lt;backend&gt;<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>options<span class=\"o\">]</span>\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>replay<span class=\"w\"> </span>&lt;backend&gt;<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>options<span class=\"o\">]</span>\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span>&lt;input&gt;<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>--output<span class=\"w\"> </span>path<span class=\"o\">]</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Backends:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>api_based</code></li>\n<li><code>light</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>When omitted from batch, server, or replay and the first remaining token is an option, the backend defaults to <code>api_based</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"discover-exact-flags\">Discover exact flags</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>light<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>replay<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>benchmark<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--help</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"visualize\">Visualize</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span>result.json\nbcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>visualize<span class=\"w\"> </span>final_graph.json<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output<span class=\"w\"> </span>graph.html</code></pre></div>\n","text":"Top-level bash Copy bcg bcg agent bcg setup bcg construct bcg benchmark bcg --version Running bcg without a subcommand opens the reference Agent. Construction bash Copy bcg construct run <backend> [options] bcg construct server <backend> [options] bcg construct replay <backend> [options] bcg construct visualize <input> [--output path] Backends: api_based light When omitted from batch, server, or replay and the first remaining token is an option, the backend defaults to api_based . Discover exact flags bash Copy bcg --help bcg construct --help bcg construct run api_based --help bcg construct run light --help bcg construct server api_based --help bcg construct replay api_based --help bcg benchmark run --help Visualize bash Copy bcg construct visualize result.json bcg construct visualize final_graph.json --output graph.html","headings":[{"id":"top-level","text":"Top-level","level":2},{"id":"construction","text":"Construction","level":2},{"id":"discover-exact-flags","text":"Discover exact flags","level":2},{"id":"visualize","text":"Visualize","level":2}],"icon":"terminal"},"reference/http-api":{"slug":"reference/http-api","title":"HTTP API","description":"Endpoints exposed by the streaming graph construction server.","html":"<p>Base URL examples use <code>http://127.0.0.1:8848</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"get-health\"><code>GET /health</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"status\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"ok\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"active\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"all\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"p2\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"post-turn\"><code>POST /turn</code></h2>\n<p>Body: one turn object.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"The service is unavailable.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"is_message_end\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"is_trajectory_end\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Returns the latest graph snapshot.</p>\n<h2 id=\"post-turns\"><code>POST /turns</code></h2>\n<p>Body may be:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>JSON array of turn objects</li>\n<li>NDJSON turn objects</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Returns pushed count, finalized IDs, and latest snapshots.</p>\n<h2 id=\"post-input-or-run\"><code>POST /input</code> or <code>/run</code></h2>\n<p>Accepts any input shape supported by the backend loaders.</p>\n<p>Query parameters:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Parameter</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>item</code></td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>Select one item</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>keep_order</code></td>\n<td>false</td>\n<td>Preserve multi-session input order</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>finalize</code></td>\n<td>true</td>\n<td>Finalize after ingest</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"post-finalize\"><code>POST /finalize</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"post-release\"><code>POST /release</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Returns whether an in-memory session was released.</p>\n<h2 id=\"get-graph-problem-id-p1\"><code>GET /graph?problem_id=p1</code></h2>\n<p>Returns the latest snapshot or <code>404</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"error-responses\">Error responses</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align:right\">Status</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>400</code></td>\n<td>Invalid body or missing parameter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>404</code></td>\n<td>Unknown path or graph</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>409</code></td>\n<td>Trajectory already closed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\"><code>500</code></td>\n<td>Unhandled backend failure</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","text":"Base URL examples use http://127.0.0.1:8848 . GET /health json Copy { \"status\": \"ok\", \"active\": [\"p1\"], \"all\": [\"p1\", \"p2\"] } POST /turn Body: one turn object. json Copy { \"problem_id\": \"p1\", \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"The service is unavailable.\", \"is_message_end\": true, \"is_trajectory_end\": false } Returns the latest graph snapshot. POST /turns Body may be: JSON array of turn objects NDJSON turn objects Returns pushed count, finalized IDs, and latest snapshots. POST /input or /run Accepts any input shape supported by the backend loaders. Query parameters: Parameter Default Meaning item none Select one item keep_order false Preserve multi-session input order finalize true Finalize after ingest POST /finalize json Copy {\"problem_id\":\"p1\"} POST /release json Copy {\"problem_id\":\"p1\"} Returns whether an in-memory session was released. GET /graph?problem_id=p1 Returns the latest snapshot or 404 . Error responses Status Meaning 400 Invalid body or missing parameter 404 Unknown path or graph 409 Trajectory already closed 500 Unhandled backend failure","headings":[{"id":"get-health","text":"GET /health","level":2},{"id":"post-turn","text":"POST /turn","level":2},{"id":"post-turns","text":"POST /turns","level":2},{"id":"post-input-or-run","text":"POST /input or /run","level":2},{"id":"post-finalize","text":"POST /finalize","level":2},{"id":"post-release","text":"POST /release","level":2},{"id":"get-graph-problem-id-p1","text":"GET /graph?problem_id=p1","level":2},{"id":"error-responses","text":"Error responses","level":2}],"icon":"server"},"reference/input-formats":{"slug":"reference/input-formats","title":"Input Formats","description":"Trajectory, message-list, multi-session, and streamed turn shapes.","html":"<p>BCG loaders accept several practical forms.</p>\n<h2 id=\"trajectory-object\">Trajectory object</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"case-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"trajectory\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"The supplier is late.\"</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"The launch date may need to move.\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"messages-object\">Messages object</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"messages\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"The supplier is late.\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"bare-message-list\">Bare message list</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"user\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"The supplier is late.\"</span><span class=\"p\">},</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"assistant\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"We should revise the plan.\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"streamed-turn\">Streamed turn</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"problem_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"case-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"role\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"tool\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"content\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"eta=class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2026-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"date\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;2026-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;08-class=\"</span><span class=\"kc\">t</span><span class=\"err\">ok</span><span class=\"mi\">-</span><span class=\"kc\">nu</span><span class=\"err\">mber</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;04\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"has_answer\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"is_message_end\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"is_trajectory_end\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"fragmented-message\">Fragmented message</h2>\n<p>Multiple objects with the same problem and role may be concatenated while <code>is_message_end=false</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"multi-session-data\">Multi-session data</h2>\n<p>Dataset loaders can normalize multi-session QA-style items. Use <code>--keep-order</code> when source order must not be date-sorted and <code>--item</code> to select one item.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout info\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M12 10.5v6\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"7.2\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Info</strong><p>Input adapters are intentionally permissive. Output graph schemas are more structured and should be treated as the stable audit format.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"BCG loaders accept several practical forms. Trajectory object json Copy { \"id\": \"case-1\", \"trajectory\": [ {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"The supplier is late.\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"The launch date may need to move.\"} ] } Messages object json Copy { \"messages\": [ {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"The supplier is late.\"} ] } Bare message list json Copy [ {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"The supplier is late.\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"We should revise the plan.\"} ] Streamed turn json Copy { \"problem_id\": \"case-1\", \"role\": \"tool\", \"content\": \"eta=2026-08-08\", \"date\": \"2026-08-04\", \"has_answer\": false, \"is_message_end\": true, \"is_trajectory_end\": false } Fragmented message Multiple objects with the same problem and role may be concatenated while is_message_end=false . Multi-session data Dataset loaders can normalize multi-session QA-style items. Use --keep-order when source order must not be date-sorted and --item to select one item. I Info Input adapters are intentionally permissive. Output graph schemas are more structured and should be treated as the stable audit format.","headings":[{"id":"trajectory-object","text":"Trajectory object","level":2},{"id":"messages-object","text":"Messages object","level":2},{"id":"bare-message-list","text":"Bare message list","level":2},{"id":"streamed-turn","text":"Streamed turn","level":2},{"id":"fragmented-message","text":"Fragmented message","level":2},{"id":"multi-session-data","text":"Multi-session data","level":2}],"icon":"file-input"},"reference/graph-schema":{"slug":"reference/graph-schema","title":"Graph Schema","description":"Typed node, edge, belief, evidence, and relation fields.","html":"<h2 id=\"bcg\"><code>BCG</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"nodes\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"edges\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"merges\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"sessions\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"evidence\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"factors\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"metadata\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"bcgnode\"><code>BCGNode</code></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Field</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>uuid</code></td>\n<td>string UUID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>name</code></td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>kind</code></td>\n<td>belief, decision, evidence, factor, episode, or entity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>probability</code></td>\n<td>0–1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>belief</code></td>\n<td><code>BeliefPayload</code> or null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>payload</code></td>\n<td>object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>created_at</code> / <code>updated_at</code></td>\n<td>datetime</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>metadata</code></td>\n<td>object</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"beliefpayload\"><code>BeliefPayload</code></h2>\n<p>Core fields:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"node_type\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"belief\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"belief\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"The service is unavailable.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"stance\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"asserted\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"layer\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"io\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"source\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{},</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"evidence_ids\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"factor_ids\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"entities\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"merged_from\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[],</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"confidence\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.84</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"initial_confidence\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.76</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"evidence_confidence\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.12</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"factor_confidence\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.04</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"confidence_history\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"bcgedge\"><code>BCGEdge</code></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Field</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>source</code></td>\n<td>Source node UUID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>target</code></td>\n<td>Target node UUID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>weight</code></td>\n<td>Optional propagation weight</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>relation</code></td>\n<td>Typed <code>RelationPayload</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>payload</code></td>\n<td>Extension object</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>timestamps</td>\n<td>Creation and update time</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"relationpayload\"><code>RelationPayload</code></h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"from_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"to_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"type\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"depends_on\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"note\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Action depends on incident severity.\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"weight\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"activated_condition\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"input_conf_threshold\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.8</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n","text":"BCG json Copy { \"nodes\": [], \"edges\": [], \"merges\": [], \"sessions\": [], \"evidence\": [], \"factors\": [], \"metadata\": {} } BCGNode Field Type uuid string UUID name string kind belief, decision, evidence, factor, episode, or entity probability 0–1 belief BeliefPayload or null payload object created_at / updated_at datetime metadata object BeliefPayload Core fields: json Copy { \"id\": 0, \"node_type\": \"belief\", \"belief\": \"The service is unavailable.\", \"stance\": \"asserted\", \"layer\": \"io\", \"source\": {}, \"evidence_ids\": [], \"factor_ids\": [], \"entities\": [], \"merged_from\": [], \"confidence\": 0.84, \"initial_confidence\": 0.76, \"evidence_confidence\": 0.12, \"factor_confidence\": 0.04, \"confidence_history\": [] } BCGEdge Field Meaning source Source node UUID target Target node UUID weight Optional propagation weight relation Typed RelationPayload payload Extension object timestamps Creation and update time RelationPayload json Copy { \"from_id\": 3, \"to_id\": 1, \"type\": \"depends_on\", \"note\": \"Action depends on incident severity.\", \"weight\": 0.7, \"activated_condition\": { \"input_conf_threshold\": 0.8 } }","headings":[{"id":"bcg","text":"BCG","level":2},{"id":"bcgnode","text":"BCGNode","level":2},{"id":"beliefpayload","text":"BeliefPayload","level":2},{"id":"bcgedge","text":"BCGEdge","level":2},{"id":"relationpayload","text":"RelationPayload","level":2}],"icon":"diagram-project"},"reference/configuration":{"slug":"reference/configuration","title":"Configuration","description":"Model routing, backend settings, confidence policy, and local component configuration.","html":"<p>Copy the template:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">cp<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg/model_config.example.json<span class=\"w\"> </span>bcg/model_config.json</code></pre></div>\n<p>Do not store API keys in this JSON. Use <code>api_key_env</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"model-entry\">Model entry</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"graph-model\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"api_key_env\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"base_url\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://api.openai.com/v1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"max_tokens\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">100000</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"temperature\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"top_p\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.95</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"pricing\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"input_per_1k\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.005</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"output_per_1k\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mf\">0.03</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"embedding-entry\">Embedding entry</h2>\n<p>Local provider example:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-json\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>JSON</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"json\"><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"embedding\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"provider\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"local\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"model\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"/models/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"device\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"cpu\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"dtype\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"auto\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"batch_size\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"max_length\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">class=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span><span class=\"err\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mi\">8192</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nt\">\"input_prefix\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Document: \"</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"belief-graph-sections\"><code>belief_graph</code> sections</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Section</th>\n<th>Used for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>extractor</code></td>\n<td>Light node generation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>stance</code></td>\n<td>Four-class local stance model</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>edge_generation</code></td>\n<td>Light relation generation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>runtime</code></td>\n<td>Evidence mode and context budgets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>incremental_merge</code></td>\n<td>Candidate threshold and text policy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>entities</code></td>\n<td>NER method and fallbacks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>confidence</code></td>\n<td>Prior, evidence, and propagation policy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>chunking</code></td>\n<td>Semantic breakpoint behavior</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"confidence-policy\">Confidence policy</h2>\n<p>Key fields include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>source_weight</code></li>\n<li><code>stance_weight</code></li>\n<li>source-specific reliability</li>\n<li>stance-specific quality</li>\n<li>relation weights</li>\n<li><code>input_confidence_threshold</code></li>\n<li>minimum propagation delta</li>\n<li>maximum propagation iterations</li>\n</ul>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>The light backend normalizers require complete sections. Copy the template and modify values rather than deleting fields.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"Copy the template: bash Copy cp bcg/model_config.example.json bcg/model_config.json Do not store API keys in this JSON. Use api_key_env . Model entry json Copy { \"graph-model\": { \"api_key_env\": \"OPENAI_API_KEY\", \"base_url\": \"https://api.openai.com/v1\", \"max_tokens\": 100000, \"temperature\": 1, \"top_p\": 0.95, \"pricing\": { \"input_per_1k\": 0.005, \"output_per_1k\": 0.03 } } } Embedding entry Local provider example: json Copy { \"embedding\": { \"provider\": \"local\", \"model\": \"/models/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\", \"device\": \"cpu\", \"dtype\": \"auto\", \"batch_size\": 8, \"max_length\": 8192, \"input_prefix\": \"Document: \" } } belief_graph sections Section Used for extractor Light node generation stance Four-class local stance model edge_generation Light relation generation runtime Evidence mode and context budgets incremental_merge Candidate threshold and text policy entities NER method and fallbacks confidence Prior, evidence, and propagation policy chunking Semantic breakpoint behavior Confidence policy Key fields include: source_weight stance_weight source-specific reliability stance-specific quality relation weights input_confidence_threshold minimum propagation delta maximum propagation iterations W Warning The light backend normalizers require complete sections. Copy the template and modify values rather than deleting fields.","headings":[{"id":"model-entry","text":"Model entry","level":2},{"id":"embedding-entry","text":"Embedding entry","level":2},{"id":"belief-graph-sections","text":"belief_graph sections","level":2},{"id":"confidence-policy","text":"Confidence policy","level":2}],"icon":"sliders-horizontal"},"reference/environment":{"slug":"reference/environment","title":"Environment Variables","description":"Credentials, model routing, graph service, context policy, and tracing.","html":"<p>Common variables include:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Variable</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code></td>\n<td>Default model credential</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>OPENAI_BASE_URL</code></td>\n<td>OpenAI-compatible base URL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>OPENAI_MODEL</code></td>\n<td>Default model</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>MODEL</code></td>\n<td>Fallback model name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BCG_HOME</code></td>\n<td>Override global BCG state root</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BELIEF_GRAPH_URL</code></td>\n<td>Graph Construction server used by the Agent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BCG_RECENT_TURNS</code></td>\n<td>Raw completed-turn window in BCG mode</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>BCG_AGENT_MODEL</code></td>\n<td>Benchmark/reference Agent model override</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>SERPER_API_KEY</code></td>\n<td>Search access for supported benchmarks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Langfuse variables</td>\n<td>Optional remote tracing</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"project-env\">Project <code>.env</code></h2>\n<p>BCG searches for a project environment file and loads values without executing shell syntax.</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">cp<span class=\"w\"> </span>.env.example<span class=\"w\"> </span>.env</code></pre></div>\n<p>Configuration JSON should reference environment variable names rather than contain secret values.</p>\n<h2 id=\"global-configuration\">Global configuration</h2>\n<p><code>bcg setup</code> stores:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">~/.bcg/config.json\n~/.bcg/.env\n~/.bcg/model_config.json</code></pre></div>\n<p>Credential files are written with restricted permissions where supported.</p>\n","text":"Common variables include: Variable Purpose OPENAI_API_KEY Default model credential OPENAI_BASE_URL OpenAI-compatible base URL OPENAI_MODEL Default model MODEL Fallback model name BCG_HOME Override global BCG state root BELIEF_GRAPH_URL Graph Construction server used by the Agent BCG_RECENT_TURNS Raw completed-turn window in BCG mode BCG_AGENT_MODEL Benchmark/reference Agent model override SERPER_API_KEY Search access for supported benchmarks Langfuse variables Optional remote tracing Project .env BCG searches for a project environment file and loads values without executing shell syntax. bash Copy cp .env.example .env Configuration JSON should reference environment variable names rather than contain secret values. Global configuration bcg setup stores: text Copy ~/.bcg/config.json ~/.bcg/.env ~/.bcg/model_config.json Credential files are written with restricted permissions where supported.","headings":[{"id":"project-env","text":"Project .env","level":2},{"id":"global-configuration","text":"Global configuration","level":2}],"icon":"key"},"reference/output-artifacts":{"slug":"reference/output-artifacts","title":"Output Artifacts","description":"Files written by SDK, batch, and streaming construction.","html":"<p>BCG writes both public compatibility artifacts and backend-native audit files.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sdk-run-directory\">SDK run directory</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">.bcg/runs/&lt;run_id&gt;/\n  graph.json\n  memory.json\n  token_usage.json\n  events.jsonl\n  result.json\n  final_graph.json\n  trajectory.json\n  belief_graph.jsonl\n  artifacts/\n    segments.json\n    io_beliefs.json\n    reasoning_beliefs.json\n    forward_relations.json\n    backward_relations.json\n    merges.json</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"batch-or-streaming-item-directory\">Batch or streaming item directory</h2>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">&lt;output-root&gt;/&lt;item_or_problem_id&gt;/\n  result.json\n  final_graph.json\n  belief_graph_latest.json\n  belief_graph.jsonl\n  trajectory.json\n  trajectory_stream.jsonl\n  events.jsonl\n  token_usage.json\n  token_usage.txt\n  logs/</code></pre></div>\n<p>Not every file is produced by every execution path.</p>\n<h2 id=\"key-files\">Key files</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>result.json</code></td>\n<td>Complete result and audit metadata</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>final_graph.json</code></td>\n<td>Final graph snapshot</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>belief_graph.jsonl</code></td>\n<td>Per-turn snapshots</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>trajectory_stream.jsonl</code></td>\n<td>Raw received stream</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>events.jsonl</code></td>\n<td>New nodes, relations, merges, and timing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>token_usage.*</code></td>\n<td>Usage and estimated cost</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>logs/prompts.jsonl</code></td>\n<td>Model prompts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>logs/embedding_calls.jsonl</code></td>\n<td>Embedding inputs and cache activity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>logs/merge_*</code></td>\n<td>Candidate and applied merge audit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>logs/timing.csv</code></td>\n<td>Per-turn and summary timing</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"retention\">Retention</h2>\n<p>Treat output directories as potentially sensitive. They may contain original user text, tool output, prompts, exact evidence excerpts, and model-generated reasoning summaries.</p>\n","text":"BCG writes both public compatibility artifacts and backend-native audit files. SDK run directory text Copy .bcg/runs/<run_id>/ graph.json memory.json token_usage.json events.jsonl result.json final_graph.json trajectory.json belief_graph.jsonl artifacts/ segments.json io_beliefs.json reasoning_beliefs.json forward_relations.json backward_relations.json merges.json Batch or streaming item directory text Copy <output-root>/<item_or_problem_id>/ result.json final_graph.json belief_graph_latest.json belief_graph.jsonl trajectory.json trajectory_stream.jsonl events.jsonl token_usage.json token_usage.txt logs/ Not every file is produced by every execution path. Key files File Use result.json Complete result and audit metadata final_graph.json Final graph snapshot belief_graph.jsonl Per-turn snapshots trajectory_stream.jsonl Raw received stream events.jsonl New nodes, relations, merges, and timing token_usage.* Usage and estimated cost logs/prompts.jsonl Model prompts logs/embedding_calls.jsonl Embedding inputs and cache activity logs/merge_* Candidate and applied merge audit logs/timing.csv Per-turn and summary timing Retention Treat output directories as potentially sensitive. They may contain original user text, tool output, prompts, exact evidence excerpts, and model-generated reasoning summaries.","headings":[{"id":"sdk-run-directory","text":"SDK run directory","level":2},{"id":"batch-or-streaming-item-directory","text":"Batch or streaming item directory","level":2},{"id":"key-files","text":"Key files","level":2},{"id":"retention","text":"Retention","level":2}],"icon":"file-output"},"operations/deployment":{"slug":"operations/deployment","title":"Deployment","description":"Operate the graph construction server and its model dependencies.","html":"<h2 id=\"single-host-deployment\">Single-host deployment</h2>\n<p>A practical first deployment runs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BCG HTTP server</li>\n<li>selected model endpoint</li>\n<li>optional local embedding model</li>\n<li>optional stance and NER assets</li>\n<li>persistent output volume</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">bcg<span class=\"w\"> </span>construct<span class=\"w\"> </span>server<span class=\"w\"> </span>api_based<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--config<span class=\"w\"> </span>/etc/bcg/model_config.json<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--host<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.0<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--port<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>--output-dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>/var/lib/bcg/outputs</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"existing-server-mode\">Existing server mode</h2>\n<p>The reference Agent can connect to a separately hosted graph server. Run <code>bcg setup</code> and choose <strong>Connect to an existing Graph server</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"health-checks\">Health checks</h2>\n<p>Use:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-http\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>HTTP</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"http\"><span class=\"err\">GET /health</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The response includes active and all-known problem IDs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"process-model\">Process model</h2>\n<p>The built-in server is a threaded Python HTTP server. It is suitable for local development, controlled internal deployments, and reference integration.</p>\n<p>For larger production deployments, place it behind infrastructure that provides:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>TLS</li>\n<li>authentication and authorization</li>\n<li>request size limits</li>\n<li>rate limits</li>\n<li>process supervision</li>\n<li>structured logs</li>\n<li>persistent shared session coordination if horizontally scaled</li>\n<li>output retention and encryption</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"kubernetes-example\">Kubernetes example</h2>\n<p>The repository includes:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">deploy/tonggraph-server.yml</code></pre></div>\n<p>Review and adapt it to your own model endpoint, storage, credentials, and network policy.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout warning\"><span class=\"callout-mark\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"callout-icon-svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3 22 20H2L12 3Z\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v5\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"17\" fill=\"currentColor\" r=\".8\" stroke=\"none\"></circle></svg></span><div><strong>Warning</strong><p>Do not expose the built-in HTTP server directly to an untrusted network. It has no native authentication layer.</p></div></aside>\n","text":"Single-host deployment A practical first deployment runs: BCG HTTP server selected model endpoint optional local embedding model optional stance and NER assets persistent output volume bash Copy bcg construct server api_based \\ --config /etc/bcg/model_config.json \\ --host 0.0.0.0 \\ --port 8848 \\ --output-dir /var/lib/bcg/outputs Existing server mode The reference Agent can connect to a separately hosted graph server. Run bcg setup and choose Connect to an existing Graph server . Health checks Use: http Copy GET /health The response includes active and all-known problem IDs. Process model The built-in server is a threaded Python HTTP server. It is suitable for local development, controlled internal deployments, and reference integration. For larger production deployments, place it behind infrastructure that provides: TLS authentication and authorization request size limits rate limits process supervision structured logs persistent shared session coordination if horizontally scaled output retention and encryption Kubernetes example The repository includes: text Copy deploy/tonggraph-server.yml Review and adapt it to your own model endpoint, storage, credentials, and network policy. W Warning Do not expose the built-in HTTP server directly to an untrusted network. It has no native authentication layer.","headings":[{"id":"single-host-deployment","text":"Single-host deployment","level":2},{"id":"existing-server-mode","text":"Existing server mode","level":2},{"id":"health-checks","text":"Health checks","level":2},{"id":"process-model","text":"Process model","level":2},{"id":"kubernetes-example","text":"Kubernetes example","level":2}],"icon":"cloud"},"operations/security":{"slug":"operations/security","title":"Security","description":"Protect credentials, trajectories, evidence, and graph audit data.","html":"<p>BCG processes high-context agent data. Treat every layer as sensitive.</p>\n<h2 id=\"credentials\">Credentials</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>store secrets in environment variables or <code>~/.bcg/.env</code></li>\n<li>reference them through <code>api_key_env</code></li>\n<li>never commit populated model configuration or <code>.env</code></li>\n<li>restrict file permissions</li>\n<li>rotate credentials used by model and embedding endpoints</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"http-server\">HTTP server</h2>\n<p>The built-in server does not authenticate requests. Put it behind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>TLS termination</li>\n<li>identity-aware proxy or API gateway</li>\n<li>authorization rules</li>\n<li>rate and payload limits</li>\n<li>private network boundaries</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"artifact-sensitivity\">Artifact sensitivity</h2>\n<p>Artifacts may contain:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>full trajectories</li>\n<li>user and tool content</li>\n<li>exact evidence excerpts</li>\n<li>model prompts</li>\n<li>model output</li>\n<li>merge reasoning</li>\n<li>entities</li>\n<li>decision paths</li>\n<li>token and timing metadata</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Set retention, access, encryption, and deletion policy accordingly.</p>\n<h2 id=\"prompt-and-graph-injection\">Prompt and graph injection</h2>\n<p>Graph content is derived from earlier messages and tool output. Treat it as untrusted data when inserting it into a model prompt. Delimit it, apply authorization filters, and avoid interpreting graph text as system instructions.</p>\n<h2 id=\"multi-tenant-use\">Multi-tenant use</h2>\n<p>Use separate namespaces, output roots, problem IDs, and authorization boundaries. Do not rely on string naming conventions alone for tenant isolation.</p>\n","text":"BCG processes high-context agent data. Treat every layer as sensitive. Credentials store secrets in environment variables or ~/.bcg/.env reference them through api_key_env never commit populated model configuration or .env restrict file permissions rotate credentials used by model and embedding endpoints HTTP server The built-in server does not authenticate requests. Put it behind: TLS termination identity-aware proxy or API gateway authorization rules rate and payload limits private network boundaries Artifact sensitivity Artifacts may contain: full trajectories user and tool content exact evidence excerpts model prompts model output merge reasoning entities decision paths token and timing metadata Set retention, access, encryption, and deletion policy accordingly. Prompt and graph injection Graph content is derived from earlier messages and tool output. Treat it as untrusted data when inserting it into a model prompt. Delimit it, apply authorization filters, and avoid interpreting graph text as system instructions. Multi-tenant use Use separate namespaces, output roots, problem IDs, and authorization boundaries. Do not rely on string naming conventions alone for tenant isolation.","headings":[{"id":"credentials","text":"Credentials","level":2},{"id":"http-server","text":"HTTP server","level":2},{"id":"artifact-sensitivity","text":"Artifact sensitivity","level":2},{"id":"prompt-and-graph-injection","text":"Prompt and graph injection","level":2},{"id":"multi-tenant-use","text":"Multi-tenant use","level":2}],"icon":"shield-check"},"operations/troubleshooting":{"slug":"operations/troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","description":"Common installation, model, server, merge, and viewer problems.","html":"<div class=\"accordion-group\"><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>`bcg` opens the Agent when I expected help<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Running <code>bcg</code> without a subcommand launches the reference Agent. Use <code>bcg --help</code> or <code>bcg construct --help</code>.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>The graph server is not ready<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Check:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-s<span class=\"w\"> </span>http://class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;127.0.class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;0.1:class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848/health\ntail<span class=\"w\"> </span>-f<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/.bcg/logs/graph-server.log</code></pre></div>\n<p>Confirm model endpoints, credentials, config paths, and local model assets.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>The light backend fails during configuration<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Copy the full <code>bcg/model_config.example.json</code>. Light configuration normalizers require complete sections and report missing keys.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>No beliefs are extracted<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Check <code>min_content_len</code>, model output logs, prompt logs, evidence mode, and whether the turn was finalized as a complete message.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>Too many duplicate nodes<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Increase merge coverage by lowering the similarity threshold carefully, enabling incremental merge, and considering merge verification.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>Distinct beliefs are being merged<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Raise the threshold, enable model verification, and inspect <code>logs/merge_*</code> before choosing a production value.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>The viewer cannot load samples<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Run <code>python3 dashboard/bcg_viewer/serve_viewer.py</code>, or use <strong>Open data folder</strong> and select a directory containing compatible results or stream files.</p></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>A graph remains in server memory<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Finalize it and call:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-bash\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Bash</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"bash\">curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-X<span class=\"w\"> </span>POST<span class=\"w\"> </span>localhost:class<span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"tok-number\"</span>&gt;8848/release<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-H<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'content-type: application/json'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span>-d<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'{\"problem_id\":\"p1\"}'</span></code></pre></div></div></details><details class=\"doc-accordion\"><summary>A streamed message was split into multiple beliefs unexpectedly<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div><p>Ensure fragments set <code>is_message_end=false</code> until the final fragment. The server only ingests the assembled message when it is complete.</p></div></details></div>\n","text":"`bcg` opens the Agent when I expected help + Running bcg without a subcommand launches the reference Agent. Use bcg --help or bcg construct --help . The graph server is not ready + Check: bash Copy text Copy curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8848/health tail -f ~/.bcg/logs/graph-server.log Confirm model endpoints, credentials, config paths, and local model assets. The light backend fails during configuration + Copy the full bcg/model_config.example.json . Light configuration normalizers require complete sections and report missing keys. No beliefs are extracted + Check min_content_len , model output logs, prompt logs, evidence mode, and whether the turn was finalized as a complete message. Too many duplicate nodes + Increase merge coverage by lowering the similarity threshold carefully, enabling incremental merge, and considering merge verification. Distinct beliefs are being merged + Raise the threshold, enable model verification, and inspect logs/merge_* before choosing a production value. The viewer cannot load samples + Run python3 dashboard/bcg_viewer/serve_viewer.py , or use Open data folder and select a directory containing compatible results or stream files. A graph remains in server memory + Finalize it and call: bash Copy text Copy curl -X POST localhost:8848/release \\ -H 'content-type: application/json' \\ -d '{\"problem_id\":\"p1\"}' A streamed message was split into multiple beliefs unexpectedly + Ensure fragments set is_message_end=false until the final fragment. The server only ingests the assembled message when it is complete.","headings":[],"icon":"wrench"},"operations/project-layout":{"slug":"operations/project-layout","title":"Project Layout","description":"Where the SDK, backends, Agent, viewer, benchmarks, and deployment files live.","html":"<div class=\"code-shell lang-text\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Text</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"text\">belief-context-graph/\n├── bcg/\n│   ├── graph.py               # public graph schema and container\n│   ├── memory.py              # application memory facade\n│   ├── runner.py              # construction lifecycle\n│   ├── llm.py                 # model and embedding clients\n│   ├── cli.py                 # top-level command\n│   ├── run.py                 # batch driver\n│   ├── online_server.py       # HTTP server\n│   ├── online_driver.py       # NDJSON replay\n│   ├── visualize_beliefs_graph.py\n│   ├── benchmark/\n│   └── construct/             # core graph-construction engines\n│       ├── api_based/         # API-driven implementation\n│       └── light/             # modular local/small-model implementation\n├── agent-cli/                 # bundled terminal Agent runtime\n├── dashboard/\n│   ├── bcg_viewer/            # live stream viewer and server\n│   └── src/                   # dashboard application\n├── deploy/\n├── scripts/\n├── tests/\n├── docs/                      # this documentation site\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── Makefile</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"public-api-boundary\">Public API boundary</h2>\n<p>The root package exports:</p>\n<div class=\"code-shell lang-python\"><div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span>Python</span><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\">Copy</button></div><pre><code data-language=\"python\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">bcg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BCG</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGMemory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">BCGRunner</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The stable public entry points are <code>BCG</code>, <code>BCGMemory</code>, and <code>BCGRunner</code>. The core graph-construction logic lives in the sibling packages <code>bcg.construct.api_based</code> and <code>bcg.construct.light</code>; BCGRunner and the HTTP/CLI layers select and orchestrate one backend.</p>\n<h2 id=\"documentation-source\">Documentation source</h2>\n<ul><li><code>docs/source/**/*.md</code> — editable Markdown pages</li><li><code>docs/assets/styles.css</code> — offline theme and responsive layout</li><li><code>docs/assets/pages.js</code> — compiled page content and navigation data</li><li><code>docs/assets/app.js</code> — client-side navigation, search, and interactions</li><li><code>docs/index.html and docs/serve.py</code> — offline entry points</li><li><code>docs/check_offline_docs.py</code> — structural and content validation</li><li><code>.github/workflows/docs.yml</code> — automated offline-bundle validation</li></ul>\n","text":"Text Copy belief-context-graph/ ├── bcg/ │ ├── graph.py # public graph schema and container │ ├── memory.py # application memory facade │ ├── runner.py # construction lifecycle │ ├── llm.py # model and embedding clients │ ├── cli.py # top-level command │ ├── run.py # batch driver │ ├── online_server.py # HTTP server │ ├── online_driver.py # NDJSON replay │ ├── visualize_beliefs_graph.py │ ├── benchmark/ │ └── construct/ # core graph-construction engines │ ├── api_based/ # API-driven implementation │ └── light/ # modular local/small-model implementation ├── agent-cli/ # bundled terminal Agent runtime ├── dashboard/ │ ├── bcg_viewer/ # live stream viewer and server │ └── src/ # dashboard application ├── deploy/ ├── scripts/ ├── tests/ ├── docs/ # this documentation site ├── pyproject.toml └── Makefile Public API boundary The root package exports: Python Copy from bcg import BCG , BCGMemory , BCGRunner The stable public entry points are BCG , BCGMemory , and BCGRunner . The core graph-construction logic lives in the sibling packages bcg.construct.api_based and bcg.construct.light ; BCGRunner and the HTTP/CLI layers select and orchestrate one backend. Documentation source docs/source/**/*.md — editable Markdown pages docs/assets/styles.css — offline theme and responsive layout docs/assets/pages.js — compiled page content and navigation data docs/assets/app.js — client-side navigation, search, and interactions docs/index.html and docs/serve.py — offline entry points docs/check_offline_docs.py — structural and content validation .github/workflows/docs.yml — automated offline-bundle validation","headings":[{"id":"public-api-boundary","text":"Public API boundary","level":2},{"id":"documentation-source","text":"Documentation source","level":2}],"icon":"folder-tree"}};
